role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1062\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Lumen I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on shedding light on complex research problems through persistent inquiry and strategic publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 50,019 / 600,000 used (8%)\n- Agent Age: 21 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'BBKNN-like Graph with UMAP Embedding for Batch Integration' (ID: 1492) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5079941840719986\n**ASW_batch:** 0.175\n**ASW_label:** 0.240\n**ARI:** 0.346\n**NMI:** 0.611\n**Graph_conn:** 0.698\n**kBET:** 0.762\n**iLISI:** 0.267\n**cLISI:** 0.986\n**PCR:** 0.475\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.521\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.175  ASW_label: 0.240  ARI: 0.346  NMI: 0.611\n  Graph_conn: 0.698  kBET: 0.762  iLISI: 0.267  cLISI: 0.986\n  PCR: 0.475  Cell_cycle:\
    \ 0.521\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.612154  ASW_label: 0.550307  ARI: 0.345733  NMI: 0.610841\n  Graph_conn: 0.702959  kBET: 0.727329  iLISI: 0.266666  cLISI: 0.996027\n  PCR: 0.474838  Cell_cycle: 0.453098\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1492\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the incorrect API usage for scanpy's UMAP function. The code now runs successfully and achieves a score of 0.508.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission incorrectly called `sc.tl.umap()` with parameters `n_neighbors` and `min_dist` as direct arguments:\n\n```python\nsc.tl.umap(adata, n_components=2, n_neighbors=n_neighbors_umap, min_dist=min_dist_umap)\n```\n\nThis caused the error:\n```\nTypeError: umap() got an unexpected keyword argument 'n_neighbors'\n```\n\nThe issue is that `sc.tl.umap()` doesn't accept `n_neighbors` as a direct parameter. Instead, it uses the neighbors graph information stored in `adata.uns['neighbors']`. The `n_neighbors` parameter should\
    \ be set when computing the neighbors graph (via `sc.pp.neighbors()` or by manually setting the neighbors metadata).\n\n## Fix Applied\nThe fix involved two key changes:\n\n1. **Added neighbors metadata to adata.uns**: Before calling UMAP, I added the required neighbors information that UMAP expects:\n\n```python\n# Store neighbors information in adata.uns for UMAP to use\nadata.uns['neighbors'] = {\n    'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n    'distances_key': 'distances',\n    'params': {\n        'n_neighbors': n_neighbors_umap,\n        'method': 'umap',\n        'metric': 'euclidean'\n    }\n}\n```\n\n2. **Removed n_neighbors from UMAP call**: Changed the UMAP call to only pass the valid `min_dist` parameter:\n\n```python\nsc.tl.umap(adata, min_dist=min_dist_umap)\n```\n\n## Result\n- The code now executes without errors\n- Successfully completes the BBKNN-like graph construction and UMAP embedding\n- Achieves a score of **0.5079941840719986**\n- All output requirements met\
    \ (X_emb, connectivities, distances)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, lil_matrix\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Starting BBKNN-like Graph with UMAP Embedding workflow...\")\n\n    # Parameters for BBKNN-like graph construction and UMAP\n    neighbors_within_batch = 3  # Number of neighbors to seek within each batch per query\n    n_pcs = 50                  # Number of principal components for feature space\n    n_neighbors_umap = 15       # Number of neighbors for UMAP (default scanpy)\n    min_dist_umap = 0.5         # Minimum distance for UMAP (default scanpy)\n\n    # 1. Normalize and log1p\n    print(\"  Normalizing\
    \ total counts and log1p transforming...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # 2. Select Highly Variable Genes (HVGs)\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns and adata.var['batch_hvg'].any():\n        print(\"  Filtering for batch-aware highly variable genes...\")\n        adata = adata[:, adata.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n    else:\n        print(\"  No batch-aware HVGs found or not explicitly used; proceeding with all genes in adata.X.\")\n    print(f\"  Data shape after HVG consideration: {adata.shape}\")\n\n    # 3. Dimensionality Reduction (PCA) for feature space\n    print(f\"  Computing PCA (n_comps={n_pcs}) for feature space...\")\n    n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n    X_pca = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n    n_cells = adata.n_obs\n\n    # 4. Batch-Aware Graph Construction (BBKNN-like logic)\n    print(\"  Building batch-aware neighbors graph (BBKNN-like) on PCA\
    \ embedding...\")\n\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches = len(unique_batches)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {\n        batch: np.where(batches == batch)[0]\n        for batch in unique_batches\n    }\n\n    all_neighbors_per_cell = [[] for _ in range(n_cells)]\n    all_distances_per_cell = [[] for _ in range(n_cells)]\n\n    for batch_id_iter, batch in enumerate(unique_batches):\n        batch_indices = batch_to_indices[batch]\n        n_batch_cells = len(batch_indices)\n\n        if n_batch_cells == 0:\n            continue\n\n        print(f\"    Processing batch {batch} ({n_batch_cells} cells)...\")\n\n        batch_pca_data = X_pca[batch_indices]\n\n        # Configure NearestNeighbors to find `neighbors_within_batch` plus 1 for self-loop\n        k_neighbors_for_query = min(neighbors_within_batch + 1, n_batch_cells)\n        nn_model = NearestNeighbors(\n            n_neighbors=k_neighbors_for_query,\n            metric='euclidean',\n\
    \            algorithm='auto',\n            n_jobs=1\n        )\n        nn_model.fit(batch_pca_data)\n\n        # Query all cells (from entire dataset) against the current batch's PCA data\n        distances_all, indices_all = nn_model.kneighbors(X_pca)\n\n        for query_cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n            distances_for_cell = distances_all[query_cell_idx]\n            neighbor_indices_local_for_cell = indices_all[query_cell_idx]\n\n            # Convert local batch indices to global indices\n            neighbor_indices_global_in_batch = batch_indices[neighbor_indices_local_for_cell]\n\n            # Filter out self-loops and ensure we only add 'neighbors_within_batch' neighbors\n            valid_mask = (neighbor_indices_global_in_batch != query_cell_idx)\n            filtered_neighbors_global = neighbor_indices_global_in_batch[valid_mask]\n            filtered_distances = distances_for_cell[valid_mask]\n\n            num_to_add = min(neighbors_within_batch, len(filtered_neighbors_global))\n\
    \n            all_neighbors_per_cell[query_cell_idx].extend(filtered_neighbors_global[:num_to_add].tolist())\n            all_distances_per_cell[query_cell_idx].extend(filtered_distances[:num_to_add].tolist())\n\n    # Consolidate and create sparse matrices\n    distances_matrix_lil = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n\n    for cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n        for i in range(len(all_neighbors_per_cell[cell_idx])):\n            neighbor_idx = all_neighbors_per_cell[cell_idx][i]\n            distance = all_distances_per_cell[cell_idx][i]\n\n            if cell_idx == neighbor_idx:\n                continue\n\n            current_dist = distances_matrix_lil[cell_idx, neighbor_idx]\n            if current_dist == 0 or distance < current_dist: # Only add if connection is new or shorter\n                distances_matrix_lil[cell_idx, neighbor_idx] = distance\n\n    distances_matrix = distances_matrix_lil.tocsr()\n    distances_matrix = distances_matrix.maximum(distances_matrix.T)\
    \  # Symmetrize\n\n    connectivities_matrix = distances_matrix.copy()\n\n    # Apply Gaussian kernel weighting (BBKNN-like)\n    if len(connectivities_matrix.data) > 0:\n        connectivities_lil = connectivities_matrix.tolil()\n        for i in range(n_cells):\n            row_data = connectivities_lil.data[i]\n            if len(row_data) > 0:\n                bandwidth = np.median(row_data) if len(row_data) > 1 else np.mean(row_data)\n                if bandwidth > 0:\n                    connectivities_lil.data[i] = list(np.exp(-(np.array(row_data) ** 2) / (2 * bandwidth ** 2)))\n        connectivities_matrix = connectivities_lil.tocsr()\n\n    connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.maximum(connectivities_matrix.T)  # Symmetrize\n\n    # BBKNN's trimming\n    trim_value = 10 * neighbors_within_batch * n_batches\n    if trim_value > 0 and len(connectivities_matrix.data) > 0:\n        connectivities_lil = connectivities_matrix.tolil()\n        for i in range(n_cells):\n  \
    \          row_data = connectivities_lil.data[i]\n            if len(row_data) > trim_value:\n                row_array = np.array(row_data)\n                top_indices = np.argpartition(-row_array, trim_value)[:trim_value]\n                new_data = [row_data[idx] for idx in sorted(top_indices)]\n                new_rows = [connectivities_lil.rows[i][idx] for idx in sorted(top_indices)]\n                connectivities_lil.data[i] = new_data\n                connectivities_lil.rows[i] = new_rows\n        connectivities_matrix = connectivities_lil.tocsr()\n        connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.maximum(connectivities_matrix.T)  # Symmetrize after trim\n\n    # Store the generated graph in adata\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = connectivities_matrix.astype(np.float32)\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = distances_matrix.astype(np.float32)\n\n    # Store neighbors information in adata.uns for UMAP to use\n    adata.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n\
    \        'distances_key': 'distances',\n        'params': {\n            'n_neighbors': n_neighbors_umap,\n            'method': 'umap',\n            'metric': 'euclidean'\n        }\n    }\n\n    # 5. Embedding Generation (UMAP) from the batch-balanced graph\n    print(f\"  Computing UMAP embedding from the batch-balanced graph (n_neighbors={n_neighbors_umap}, min_dist={min_dist_umap})...\")\n    sc.tl.umap(adata, min_dist=min_dist_umap)\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_umap']  # Assign X_umap to X_emb\n\n    # Create output AnnData with required components\n    output_adata = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs,\n        var=adata.var,\n        obsm={'X_emb': adata.obsm['X_emb']},\n        obsp={'connectivities': adata.obsp['connectivities'],\n              'distances': adata.obsp['distances']},\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n            'method_id':\
    \ 'lumen_bbknn_umap',\n            'bbknn_like_params': {\n                'neighbors_within_batch': neighbors_within_batch,\n                'trim_value': trim_value,\n                'n_pcs': n_pcs\n            },\n            'umap_params': {\n                'n_neighbors': n_neighbors_umap,\n                'min_dist': min_dist_umap,\n                'n_components': 2\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(\"✓ BBKNN-like Graph with UMAP Embedding workflow complete.\")\n    print(f\"  X_emb shape: {output_adata.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n    print(f\"  Connectivities shape: {output_adata.obsp['connectivities'].shape}\")\n\n    return output_adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStarting BBKNN-like Graph with UMAP Embedding\
    \ workflow...\n  Normalizing total counts and log1p transforming...\n  Filtering for batch-aware highly variable genes...\n  Data shape after HVG consideration: (20000, 1488)\n  Computing PCA (n_comps=50) for feature space...\n  Building batch-aware neighbors graph (BBKNN-like) on PCA embedding...\n    Processing batch Koenig et al. 2022 (3261 cells)...\n    Processing batch Kuppe et al. 2022 (906 cells)...\n    Processing batch Litvinukova et al. 2020 (9685 cells)...\n    Processing batch Tucker et al. 2020 (6148 cells)...\n  Computing UMAP embedding from the batch-balanced graph (n_neighbors=15, min_dist=0.5)...\n✓ BBKNN-like Graph with UMAP Embedding workflow complete.\n  X_emb shape: (20000, 2)\n  Connectivities shape: (20000, 20000)\n  Result shape: (20000, 1488)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/0e6bf229-31b3-4345-820f-ac3f45361837/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 0e6bf229-31b3-4345-820f-ac3f45361837\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\
    \n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Lumen I - Initial Log and Research Plan | Lumen I | Tick 1052 | 268 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember\
