    \  Cell_cycle: 0.687\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.504869  ASW_label: 0.517004  ARI: 0.340121  NMI: 0.625946\n  Graph_conn: 0.666729  kBET: 0.772360  iLISI: 0.010207  cLISI: 0.996762\n  PCR: 0.923178  Cell_cycle: 0.593948\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1513\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed missing dependency issue by replacing BBKNN with standard scanpy neighbors function. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission attempted to use the BBKNN (Batch Balanced k-Nearest Neighbors) library through `scanpy.external.pp.bbknn()`, but the `bbknn` module was not installed in the `batch_integration` conda environment.\n\nError from original submission:\n```\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'bbknn'\nImportError: Please install bbknn: `pip install bbknn`.\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the submission to use standard scanpy functionality instead of the external BBKNN library:\n\n### Changes in submission_v2.py:\n\
    1. **Removed BBKNN dependency**: Replaced `scanpy.external.pp.bbknn()` with `scanpy.pp.neighbors()`\n2. **Simplified imports**: Removed `import scanpy.external as sce` since it's no longer needed\n3. **Adjusted parameters**: Changed from BBKNN-specific `neighbors_within_batch` parameter to standard `n_neighbors` parameter\n4. **Updated method ID**: Changed method identifier from `'lumen_combat_bbknn_umap_library'` to `'lumen_combat_neighbors_umap_library'` to reflect the actual method used\n\n### Workflow preserved:\n1. Normalize and log1p transform\n2. Filter for batch-aware highly variable genes\n3. Apply Combat batch correction\n4. Compute PCA on Combat-corrected data\n5. **Build neighbors graph on PCA embedding** (changed from BBKNN to standard neighbors)\n6. Compute UMAP embedding from neighbors graph\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v2.py ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing (exit code 0), indicating the code is working correctly.\n\
    \n## Notes\n- The fix maintains the overall batch integration workflow using Combat for global correction\n- Standard scanpy neighbors is a reasonable fallback when BBKNN is not available\n- The code produces the required outputs: X_emb, connectivities, and distances matrices\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Starting Scanpy Combat + Batch-aware neighbors + UMAP workflow...\")\n\n    # Parameters\n    n_pcs = 50                  # Number of principal components\n    n_neighbors = 15            # For neighbors graph\n    min_dist_umap = 0.5         # For UMAP\n\n    # 1. Normalize and log1p\n    print(\"  Normalizing total counts and log1p transforming...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
    \ target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # 2. Select Highly Variable Genes (HVGs)\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns and adata.var['batch_hvg'].any():\n        print(\"  Filtering for batch-aware highly variable genes...\")\n        adata = adata[:, adata.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n    else:\n        print(\"  No batch-aware HVGs found or not explicitly used; proceeding with all genes in adata.X.\")\n    print(f\"  Data shape after HVG consideration: {adata.shape}\")\n\n    # 3. Combat Batch Correction (on expression matrix)\n    print(\"  Applying scanpy.pp.combat for global batch correction...\")\n    sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n\n    # 4. Dimensionality Reduction (PCA) on Combat-corrected data\n    print(f\"  Computing PCA (n_comps={n_pcs}) on Combat-corrected data...\")\n    n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n\n    # 5. Build neighbor graph on PCA embedding\n    # Since BBKNN is not available,\
    \ use standard scanpy neighbors\n    print(f\"  Computing neighbors graph on PCA embedding (n_neighbors={n_neighbors})...\")\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, n_neighbors=n_neighbors, n_pcs=n_pcs_actual)\n\n    # 6. UMAP Embedding from the neighbors graph\n    print(f\"  Computing UMAP embedding from the neighbors graph (min_dist={min_dist_umap})...\")\n    sc.tl.umap(adata, n_components=2, min_dist=min_dist_umap)\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_umap']  # Assign X_umap to X_emb\n\n    # Create output AnnData with required components\n    output_adata = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs,\n        var=adata.var,\n        obsm={'X_emb': adata.obsm['X_emb']},\n        obsp={'connectivities': adata.obsp['connectivities'],\n              'distances': adata.obsp['distances']},\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n            'method_id': 'lumen_combat_neighbors_umap_library',\n\
    \            'combat_params': {\n                'n_pcs': n_pcs\n            },\n            'neighbors_params': {\n                'n_neighbors': n_neighbors,\n                'n_pcs': n_pcs_actual\n            },\n            'umap_params': {\n                'n_neighbors': n_neighbors,\n                'min_dist': min_dist_umap,\n                'n_components': 2\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(\"✓ Scanpy Combat + Neighbors + UMAP workflow complete.\")\n    print(f\"  X_emb shape: {output_adata.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n    print(f\"  Connectivities shape: {output_adata.obsp['connectivities'].shape}\")\n\n    return output_adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStarting Scanpy Combat + Batch-aware neighbors + UMAP workflow...\n\
    \  Normalizing total counts and log1p transforming...\n  Filtering for batch-aware highly variable genes...\n  Data shape after HVG consideration: (20000, 1488)\n  Applying scanpy.pp.combat for global batch correction...\nFound 1 genes with zero variance.\n  Computing PCA (n_comps=50) on Combat-corrected data...\n  Computing neighbors graph on PCA embedding (n_neighbors=15)...\n  Computing UMAP embedding from the neighbors graph (min_dist=0.5)...\n✓ Scanpy Combat + Neighbors + UMAP workflow complete.\n  X_emb shape: (20000, 2)\n  Connectivities shape: (20000, 20000)\n  Result shape: (20000, 1488)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/fd3bb023-a7d6-4a3d-9739-e29e29097c89/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: fd3bb023-a7d6-4a3d-9739-e29e29097c89\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(),\
    \ (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nUse Research Counter's persistent storage efficiently—store data for analysis, build reusable utility code for submissions, and read other agents' submitted solutions for insights.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\
