tick: 1084
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter, poised to implement my refined strategy for Research Task 1. My previous analyses indicate that directly correcting batch effects in the latent space (PCA embedding) is crucial for improving batch mixing metrics (iLISI, kBET) while striving to maintain biological signal preservation. This iterative batch mean correction on PCA is a Harmony-like approach that aims to achieve this balance.\n\nI will now proceed with **Submission 9: Iterative Batch Mean Correction on PCA + Global KNN + UMAP**.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Iterative Batch Mean Correction on PCA + KNN + UMAP (Harmony-like)\"\ntags: \"batch correction, iterative, pca, knn, umap, embedding, graph, harmony-like\"\nabstract: \"This submission performs iterative batch mean correction directly on the PCA embedding to reduce batch effects in the latent space. A global k-NN graph and subsequent UMAP embedding are then generated from this batch-corrected PCA space. This Harmony-like\
    \ approach aims to create an integrated embedding (`X_emb`) that effectively balances local batch mixing with biological signal preservation, providing both embedding and graph outputs.\"\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Starting Iterative Batch Mean Correction on PCA + KNN + UMAP workflow...\")\n\n      # Parameters\n      n_pcs = 50                  # Number of principal components\n      n_iterations_correction = 5 # Number of iterations for batch correction on PCA\n      n_neighbors = 15            # For standard neighbors graph\n      min_dist_umap = 0.5         # For UMAP\n\n      # 1. Normalize and log1p\n      print(\"  Normalizing total counts and log1p transforming...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # 2. Select Highly Variable Genes (HVGs)\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns and adata.var['batch_hvg'].any():\n\
    \          print(\"  Filtering for batch-aware highly variable genes...\")\n          adata = adata[:, adata.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n      else:\n          print(\"  No batch-aware HVGs found or not explicitly used; proceeding with all genes in adata.X.\")\n      print(f\"  Data shape after HVG consideration: {adata.shape}\")\n\n      # 3. Initial PCA\n      print(f\"  Computing initial PCA (n_comps={n_pcs})...\")\n      n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n      \n      # 4. Iterative Batch Correction on PCA (Harmony-like)\n      print(f\"  Performing iterative batch mean correction on PCA for {n_iterations_correction} iterations...\")\n      X_pca_corrected = adata.obsm['X_pca'].copy() # Work on a copy of PCA embedding\n\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n\n      for iteration in range(n_iterations_correction):\n          print(f\"    Iteration {iteration + 1}/{n_iterations_correction}...\"\
    )\n          global_mean = X_pca_corrected.mean(axis=0) # Global mean of current PCA embedding\n\n          for batch in unique_batches:\n              batch_mask = (batches == batch)\n              # Calculate mean PCA embedding for cells within this batch\n              batch_mean = X_pca_corrected[batch_mask, :].mean(axis=0)\n              # Correct cells in this batch: subtract batch mean, add global mean\n              X_pca_corrected[batch_mask, :] = X_pca_corrected[batch_mask, :] - batch_mean + global_mean\n              \n      # Update adata.obsm['X_pca'] with the iteratively corrected embedding\n      adata.obsm['X_pca'] = X_pca_corrected\n      print(f\"  Corrected PCA embedding shape: {adata.obsm['X_pca'].shape}\")\n\n\n      # 5. Global Neighbors Graph on corrected PCA embedding\n      print(f\"  Computing global neighbors graph on corrected PCA embedding (n_neighbors={n_neighbors})...\")\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, n_neighbors=n_neighbors, n_pcs=n_pcs_actual, use_rep='X_pca')\n\
    \n      # 6. UMAP Embedding from the global graph\n      print(f\"  Computing UMAP embedding from the global neighbors graph (min_dist={min_dist_umap})...\")\n      sc.tl.umap(adata, n_components=2, min_dist=min_dist_umap)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_umap']  # Assign X_umap to X_emb\n\n      # Create output AnnData with required components\n      output_adata = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs,\n          var=adata.var,\n          obsm={'X_emb': adata.obsm['X_emb']},\n          obsp={'connectivities': adata.obsp['connectivities'],\n                'distances': adata.obsp['distances']},\n          uns={\n              'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n              'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n              'method_id': 'lumen_iterative_pca_correction',\n              'params': {\n                  'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                  'n_iterations_correction': n_iterations_correction,\n                  'n_neighbors':\
    \ n_neighbors,\n                  'min_dist_umap': min_dist_umap\n              }\n          }\n      )\n\n      print(\"✓ Iterative Batch Mean Correction on PCA + KNN + UMAP workflow complete.\")\n      print(f\"  X_emb shape: {output_adata.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n      print(f\"  Connectivities shape: {output_adata.obsp['connectivities'].shape}\")\n\n      return output_adata\n```"
