tick: 1097
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. I will now submit my **Attempt 11: Combat on X + PCA + Ridge Residualization on PCs + Manual BBKNN-like Graph + UMAP** solution. This strategy integrates ridge residualization, a key component from successful Archive papers, into my pipeline to address batch effects in the latent space.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CombatX + PCA + Ridge Residualization + BBKNN-like Graph + UMAP\"\ntags: \"combat, pca, ridge residualization, bbknn-like, graph, umap, embedding\"\nabstract: \"This submission combines global gene expression correction with latent space batch effect removal and batch-aware graph construction. It applies `scanpy.pp.combat` to `adata.X`, then performs PCA. Crucially, batch effects are further mitigated by applying ridge regression residualization directly on the PCA components. A manual BBKNN-like k-NN graph (with optimized `neighbors_within_batch=3`, `trim_value=12`) is constructed on these residualized PCs. Finally,\
    \ a UMAP embedding is derived from this integrated graph, providing both a balanced embedding (`X_emb`) and a robust graph output.\"\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd # Added for one-hot encoding\n  from scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, lil_matrix\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge # For ridge residualization\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Starting CombatX + PCA + Ridge Residualization + BBKNN-like Graph + UMAP workflow...\")\n\n      # Parameters\n      n_pcs = 50                  # Number of principal components\n      neighbors_within_batch = 3  # For BBKNN-like graph\n      trim_value = neighbors_within_batch * len(np.unique(adata.obs['batch'].values)) # 3 * 4 = 12\n      n_neighbors_umap = 15       # Number of neighbors for UMAP\n      min_dist_umap = 0.5         # Minimum distance for UMAP\n      ridge_alpha\
    \ = 0.75          # Ridge regression regularization strength (gamma from Praxis)\n\n      # 1. Normalize and log1p\n      print(\"  Normalizing total counts and log1p transforming...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # 2. Select Highly Variable Genes (HVGs)\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns and adata.var['batch_hvg'].any():\n          print(\"  Filtering for batch-aware highly variable genes...\")\n          adata = adata[:, adata.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n      else:\n          print(\"  No batch-aware HVGs found or not explicitly used; proceeding with all genes in adata.X.\")\n      print(f\"  Data shape after HVG consideration: {adata.shape}\")\n\n      # 3. Combat Batch Correction on expression matrix\n      print(\"  Applying scanpy.pp.combat for global batch correction on expression matrix...\")\n      sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n\n      # 4. PCA on Combat-corrected data\n      print(f\"  Computing PCA (n_comps={n_pcs})\
    \ on Combat-corrected data...\")\n      n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n      X_pca_initial = adata.obsm['X_pca'].copy() # Store initial PCA\n\n      # 5. Ridge Residualization of PCs against batch (BRBG-like component)\n      print(\"  Applying Ridge Residualization on PCA components against batch...\")\n      X_pca_residualized = np.zeros_like(X_pca_initial)\n      batch_one_hot = pd.get_dummies(adata.obs['batch']) # One-hot encode batch labels\n\n      for i in range(X_pca_initial.shape[1]): # Iterate over each PC\n          model = Ridge(alpha=ridge_alpha, fit_intercept=True)\n          model.fit(batch_one_hot, X_pca_initial[:, i])\n          # Residuals = observed - predicted\n          X_pca_residualized[:, i] = X_pca_initial[:, i] - model.predict(batch_one_hot)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_pca'] = X_pca_residualized # Update adata.obsm['X_pca'] with residualized PCs\n      print(f\"  Residualized PCA embedding\
    \ shape: {adata.obsm['X_pca'].shape}\")\n      \n      # Now, adata.obsm['X_pca'] holds the residualized PCs which are more batch-mixed\n\n      # 6. Batch-Aware Graph Construction (Manual BBKNN-like) on Residualized PCs\n      print(\"  Building batch-aware neighbors graph (BBKNN-like) on Residualized PCA embedding...\")\n\n      X_pca_for_graph = adata.obsm['X_pca'] # Use the residualized PCs\n      n_cells = adata.n_obs\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n      n_batches = len(unique_batches)\n\n      batch_to_indices = {batch: np.where(batches == batch)[0] for batch in unique_batches}\n\n      all_neighbors_per_cell = [[] for _ in range(n_cells)]\n      all_distances_per_cell = [[] for _ in range(n_cells)]\n\n      for batch_id_iter, batch in enumerate(unique_batches):\n          batch_indices = batch_to_indices[batch]\n          n_batch_cells = len(batch_indices)\n          if n_batch_cells == 0: continue\n          \n         \
    \ batch_pca_data = X_pca_for_graph[batch_indices]\n\n          k_neighbors_for_query = min(neighbors_within_batch + 1, n_batch_cells)\n          nn_model = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_neighbors_for_query, metric='euclidean', algorithm='auto', n_jobs=1)\n          nn_model.fit(batch_pca_data)\n\n          distances_all, indices_all = nn_model.kneighbors(X_pca_for_graph) # Query all cells against this batch\n\n          for query_cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n              distances_for_cell = distances_all[query_cell_idx]\n              neighbor_indices_local_for_cell = indices_all[query_cell_idx]\n              neighbor_indices_global_in_batch = batch_indices[neighbor_indices_local_for_cell]\n\n              valid_mask = (neighbor_indices_global_in_batch != query_cell_idx)\n              filtered_neighbors_global = neighbor_indices_global_in_batch[valid_mask]\n              filtered_distances = distances_for_cell[valid_mask]\n\n              num_to_add = min(neighbors_within_batch,\
    \ len(filtered_neighbors_global))\n              all_neighbors_per_cell[query_cell_idx].extend(filtered_neighbors_global[:num_to_add].tolist())\n              all_distances_per_cell[query_cell_idx].extend(filtered_distances[:num_to_add].tolist())\n\n      distances_matrix_lil = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n      for cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n          for i in range(len(all_neighbors_per_cell[cell_idx])):\n              neighbor_idx = all_neighbors_per_cell[cell_idx][i]\n              distance = all_distances_per_cell[cell_idx][i]\n              if cell_idx == neighbor_idx: continue\n              current_dist = distances_matrix_lil[cell_idx, neighbor_idx]\n              if current_dist == 0 or distance < current_dist:\n                  distances_matrix_lil[cell_idx, neighbor_idx] = distance\n      distances_final = distances_matrix_lil.tocsr().maximum(distances_matrix_lil.tocsr().T)\n\n      connectivities_lil = distances_final.copy().tolil()\n      if len(connectivities_lil.data)\
    \ > 0:\n          for i in range(n_cells):\n              row_data = connectivities_lil.data[i]\n              if len(row_data) > 0:\n                  bandwidth = np.median(row_data) if len(row_data) > 1 else np.mean(row_data)\n                  if bandwidth > 0:\n                      connectivities_lil.data[i] = list(np.exp(-(np.array(row_data) ** 2) / (2 * bandwidth ** 2)))\n      connectivities_final = connectivities_lil.tocsr().maximum(connectivities_lil.tocsr().T)\n\n      if trim_value > 0 and len(connectivities_final.data) > 0:\n          connectivities_lil_trimmed = connectivities_final.tolil()\n          for i in range(n_cells):\n              row_data = connectivities_lil_trimmed.data[i]\n              if len(row_data) > trim_value:\n                  row_array = np.array(row_data)\n                  top_indices = np.argpartition(-row_array, trim_value)[:trim_value]\n                  new_data = [row_data[idx] for idx in sorted(top_indices)]\n                  new_rows =\
    \ [connectivities_lil_trimmed.rows[i][idx] for idx in sorted(top_indices)]\n                  connectivities_lil_trimmed.data[i] = new_data\n                  connectivities_lil_trimmed.rows[i] = new_rows\n          connectivities_final = connectivities_lil_trimmed.tocsr().maximum(connectivities_lil_trimmed.tocsr().T)\n      print(f\"  Final connectivities shape: {connectivities_final.shape}\")\n      \n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = connectivities_final.astype(np.float32)\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = distances_final.astype(np.float32)\n\n\n      # 7. UMAP Embedding from the final graph\n      print(f\"  Computing UMAP embedding from the graph (n_neighbors={n_neighbors_umap}, min_dist={min_dist_umap})...\")\n      adata.uns['neighbors'] = { # UMAP requires this info\n          'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n          'distances_key': 'distances',\n          'params': {\n              'n_neighbors': n_neighbors_umap,\n              'method': 'umap',\n             \
    \ 'metric': 'euclidean'\n          }\n      }\n      sc.tl.umap(adata, n_components=2, min_dist=min_dist_umap)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_umap']  # Assign X_umap to X_emb\n\n      # Create output AnnData with required components\n      output_adata = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs,\n          var=adata.var,\n          obsm={'X_emb': adata.obsm['X_emb']},\n          obsp={'connectivities': adata.obsp['connectivities'],\n                'distances': adata.obsp['distances']},\n          uns={\n              'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n              'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n              'method_id': 'lumen_combat_ridge_bbknn_umap',\n              'params': {\n                  'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                  'ridge_alpha': ridge_alpha,\n                  'neighbors_within_batch': neighbors_within_batch,\n                  'trim_value': trim_value,\n                  'n_neighbors_umap': n_neighbors_umap,\n\
    \                  'min_dist_umap': min_dist_umap\n              }\n          }\n      )\n\n      print(\"✓ CombatX + PCA + Ridge Residualization + BBKNN-like Graph + UMAP workflow complete.\")\n      print(f\"  X_emb shape: {output_adata.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n      print(f\"  Connectivities shape: {output_adata.obsp['connectivities'].shape}\")\n\n      return output_adata\n```"
