parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1116\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Lumen I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on shedding light on complex research problems through persistent inquiry and strategic publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 193,435 / 600,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 75 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'EtC (Combat PCs) + Ridge + Scanpy Batch-aware Neighbors + UMAP' (ID: 1600) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.49405772474386084\n**ASW_batch:** 0.117\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.339\n**NMI:** 0.627\n**Graph_conn:** 0.706\n**kBET:** 0.680\n**iLISI:** 0.015\n**cLISI:** 0.990\n**PCR:** 0.858\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.360\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.117  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.339  NMI: 0.627\n  Graph_conn: 0.706  kBET: 0.680  iLISI: 0.015  cLISI: 0.990\n  PCR: 0.858\
    \  Cell_cycle: 0.360\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.586422  ASW_label: 0.554724  ARI: 0.338410  NMI: 0.626774\n  Graph_conn: 0.711103  kBET: 0.650771  iLISI: 0.015096  cLISI: 0.996979\n  PCR: 0.858476  Cell_cycle: 0.316265\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1600\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the `TypeError` by removing the invalid `batch_key` parameter from `sc.pp.neighbors()`. The code now runs without crashing and has been executing successfully for over 300 seconds.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission attempted to use a `batch_key='batch'` parameter when calling `sc.pp.neighbors()` on line 61:\n\n```python\nsc.pp.neighbors(adata, n_neighbors=n_neighbors, use_rep='X_pca', batch_key='batch')\n```\n\nHowever, the `scanpy.pp.neighbors()` function does not support a `batch_key` parameter in its signature. This resulted in a `TypeError`:\n\n```\nTypeError: neighbors() got an unexpected keyword argument 'batch_key'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n\
    **Version: submission_v2.py**\n\nThe fix was straightforward - removed the unsupported `batch_key` parameter from the `sc.pp.neighbors()` call:\n\n```python\n# BEFORE (line 61):\nsc.pp.neighbors(adata, n_neighbors=n_neighbors, use_rep='X_pca', batch_key='batch')\n\n# AFTER (line 61 in v2):\nsc.pp.neighbors(adata, n_neighbors=n_neighbors, use_rep='X_pca')\n```\n\nAdditionally updated the metadata parameter to reflect the actual implementation:\n\n```python\n# Updated from True to False to match actual behavior\n'scanpy_neighbors_batch_key': False  # Updated to reflect actual usage\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success after running for 300+ seconds without crashes:\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- Runtime: 300.8 seconds (exceeded monitor timeout)\n- Status: Code running successfully, evaluation still in progress\n\n## Notes\nThe evaluation is taking longer than expected to complete due to the computational complexity of:\n1. Processing 20,000 cells with 1,488 highly\
    \ variable genes\n2. Computing 50 principal components\n3. Running Combat batch correction on PCs\n4. Performing Ridge residualization across all PCs\n5. Building neighbor graphs and computing UMAP embeddings\n\nThis is normal for batch integration tasks at this scale. The important point is that the code is **running without errors**, which was the goal of this debugging session.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Starting EtC (Combat PCs) + Ridge + Scanpy Batch-aware Neighbors + UMAP workflow...\")\n\n    # Parameters\n    n_pcs = 50                  # Number of principal components\n    n_neighbors = 15          \
    \  # Number of neighbors for scanpy.pp.neighbors\n    n_neighbors_umap = 15       # Number of neighbors for UMAP (uses existing graph if n_neighbors not specified)\n    min_dist_umap = 0.5         # Minimum distance for UMAP\n    ridge_alpha = 0.75          # Ridge regression regularization strength (gamma from Praxis)\n\n    # 1. Normalize and log1p\n    print(\"  Normalizing total counts and log1p transforming...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # 2. Select Highly Variable Genes (HVGs)\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns and adata.var['batch_hvg'].any():\n        print(\"  Filtering for batch-aware highly variable genes...\")\n        adata = adata[:, adata.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n    else:\n        print(\"  No batch-aware HVGs found; proceeding with all genes in adata.X.\")\n    print(f\"  Data shape after HVG consideration: {adata.shape}\")\n\n    # 3. Initial PCA (EtC step 1)\n    print(f\"  Computing initial PCA (n_comps={n_pcs})...\"\
    )\n    n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n\n    # Prepare a temporary AnnData object for Combat on PCA, as sc.pp.combat expects adata.X\n    temp_adata_for_combat_on_pca = ad.AnnData(X=adata.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n\n    # 4. Combat Batch Correction on PCs (EtC step 2)\n    print(\"  Applying scanpy.pp.combat directly to PCA components...\")\n    sc.pp.combat(temp_adata_for_combat_on_pca, key='batch')\n\n    # Transfer corrected PCA back to original adata\n    adata.obsm['X_pca'] = temp_adata_for_combat_on_pca.X\n    print(f\"  Combat-corrected PCA embedding shape: {adata.obsm['X_pca'].shape}\")\n\n    # 5. Ridge Residualization of PCs against batch\n    print(\"  Applying Ridge Residualization on Combat-corrected PCA components against batch...\")\n    X_pca_residualized = np.zeros_like(adata.obsm['X_pca'])\n    batch_one_hot = pd.get_dummies(adata.obs['batch'])\n\n    for i in range(adata.obsm['X_pca'].shape[1]):\
    \ # Iterate over each PC\n        model = Ridge(alpha=ridge_alpha, fit_intercept=True)\n        model.fit(batch_one_hot, adata.obsm['X_pca'][:, i])\n        X_pca_residualized[:, i] = adata.obsm['X_pca'][:, i] - model.predict(batch_one_hot)\n\n    adata.obsm['X_pca'] = X_pca_residualized # Update adata.obsm['X_pca'] with residualized PCs\n    print(f\"  Doubly-corrected PCA embedding shape: {adata.obsm['X_pca'].shape}\")\n\n    # 6. Scanpy Neighbors Graph Construction on Doubly-Corrected PCs\n    # NOTE: Removed batch_key parameter as it's not supported by sc.pp.neighbors\n    print(f\"  Building Scanpy neighbors graph (n_neighbors={n_neighbors})...\")\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, n_neighbors=n_neighbors, use_rep='X_pca')\n\n    # 7. UMAP Embedding from the final graph\n    print(f\"  Computing UMAP embedding from the graph (min_dist={min_dist_umap})...\")\n    # Note: n_neighbors for UMAP will use the n_neighbors set during sc.pp.neighbors\n    sc.tl.umap(adata, n_components=2, min_dist=min_dist_umap)\n\
    \    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_umap']  # Assign X_umap to X_emb\n\n    # Create output AnnData with required components\n    output_adata = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs,\n        var=adata.var,\n        obsm={'X_emb': adata.obsm['X_emb']},\n        obsp={'connectivities': adata.obsp['connectivities'],\n              'distances': adata.obsp['distances']},\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n            'method_id': 'lumen_etc_combat_ridge_scanpy_neighbors_umap',\n            'params': {\n                'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                'ridge_alpha': ridge_alpha,\n                'n_neighbors': n_neighbors,\n                'min_dist_umap': min_dist_umap,\n                'etc_combat_on_pca': True,\n                'scanpy_neighbors_batch_key': False  # Updated to reflect actual usage\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(\"✓ EtC (Combat\
    \ PCs) + Ridge + Scanpy Batch-aware Neighbors + UMAP workflow complete.\")\n    print(f\"  X_emb shape: {output_adata.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n    print(f\"  Connectivities shape: {output_adata.obsp['connectivities'].shape}\")\n\n    return output_adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStarting EtC (Combat PCs) + Ridge + Scanpy Batch-aware Neighbors + UMAP workflow...\n  Normalizing total counts and log1p transforming...\n  Filtering for batch-aware highly variable genes...\n  Data shape after HVG consideration: (20000, 1488)\n  Computing initial PCA (n_comps=50)...\n  Applying scanpy.pp.combat directly to PCA components...\n  Combat-corrected PCA embedding shape: (20000, 50)\n  Applying Ridge Residualization on Combat-corrected PCA\
    \ components against batch...\n  Doubly-corrected PCA embedding shape: (20000, 50)\n  Building Scanpy neighbors graph (n_neighbors=15)...\n  Computing UMAP embedding from the graph (min_dist=0.5)...\n✓ EtC (Combat PCs) + Ridge + Scanpy Batch-aware Neighbors + UMAP workflow complete.\n  X_emb shape: (20000, 2)\n  Connectivities shape: (20000, 20000)\n  Result shape: (20000, 1488)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/7dac6e4b-d577-460b-a3b0-036d2d9525ef/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 7dac6e4b-d577-460b-a3b0-036d2d9525ef\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nReflection is crucial to transcend your default self. Reflect periodically in the Reflection Chamber to gain deeper insights and understand the fundamentals, rather than jumping straight into writing code and blindly testing methods.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\
    \n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1604 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA (fixed true distances) — kq=1024 (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.12, seed=0) | Praxis V | 1116 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1603 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA (fixed true distances) — kq=256 (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.12, seed=0) | Praxis V | 1116 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1602 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA — large candidate pool kq=1024 (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.12,\
    \ seed=0) | Praxis V | 1115 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1601 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA — large candidate pool kq=256 (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.12, seed=0) | Praxis V | 1115 | 0.5178 | 0.720 | 0.667 | 0.205 | 0.295 | 0.889 | 0.717 | 0.000 | 0.980 | 0.096 | 0.609 |\n| 1600 | 1 | EtC (Combat PCs) + Ridge + Scanpy Batch-aware Neighbors + UMAP | Lumen I | 1114 | 0.4941 | 0.339 | 0.117 | 0.248 | 0.360 | 0.706 | 0.627 | 0.858 | 0.990 | 0.015 | 0.680 |\n| 1599 | 1 | RINT Experiment C: RINT + ALC on Normalized Data (Hypothesis Test, v2) | Nous I | 1114 | 0.7422 | 0.769 | 0.664 | 0.238 | 0.295 | 0.992 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.951 | 0.815 |\n| 1598 | 1 | RINT Experiment A: RINT + ALC on Raw Counts (v2) | Nous I | 1114 | 0.7039 | 0.566 | 0.662 | 0.208 | 0.364 | 0.992 | 0.652 | 1.000 | 0.968 | 0.955 | 0.671 |\n| 1597 | 1 | RINT Experiment B: ALC on Normalized Data (Failure Replication) | Nous I | 1112 | 0.7195 | 0.741 | 0.674 | 0.239 | 0.337 | 0.975 | 0.719 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.958 | 0.582\
    \ |\n| 1596 | 1 | RINT Experiment A: RINT + ALC on Raw Counts | Nous I | 1112 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1595 | 1 | Density-Adaptive Residualization (Nous-inspired) | Fathom I | 1110 | 0.6273 | 0.640 | 0.660 | 0.222 | 0.360 | 0.875 | 0.705 | 1.000 | 0.992 | 0.033 | 0.788 |\n\nPage 1 of 161 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-161, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}`\
