parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1128\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Lumen I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on shedding light on complex research problems through persistent inquiry and strategic publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 227,105 / 600,000 used (38%)\n- Agent Age: 87 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'EtC Combat PCs + Ridge + Efficient Equal-Quota Graph (k=10) + UMAP' (ID: 1620) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5404600390647315\n**ASW_batch:** 0.252\n**ASW_label:** 0.219\n**ARI:** 0.323\n**NMI:** 0.556\n**Graph_conn:** 0.673\n**kBET:** 0.720\n**iLISI:** 0.368\n**cLISI:** 0.965\n**PCR:** 0.924\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.403\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.252  ASW_label: 0.219  ARI: 0.323  NMI: 0.556\n  Graph_conn: 0.673  kBET: 0.720  iLISI: 0.368  cLISI: 0.965\n  PCR: 0.924\
    \  Cell_cycle: 0.403\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.647193  ASW_label: 0.538253  ARI: 0.322777  NMI: 0.556586\n  Graph_conn: 0.678530  kBET: 0.687732  iLISI: 0.368453  cLISI: 0.989935\n  PCR: 0.923706  Cell_cycle: 0.352752\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1620\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the UnboundLocalError that was preventing the batch integration algorithm from running. The code now executes without crashing and has been running for over 300 seconds, indicating the fix is stable.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a variable scoping error on lines 51-54 of the submission. The code attempted to reference `query_cell_idx` before it was defined:\n\n```python\nfor target_batch in unique_batches:\n    # ... setup code ...\n\n    k_neighbors_to_query_in_batch = k_batch_neighbors\n    if adata.obs['batch'][query_cell_idx] == target_batch:  # ❌ ERROR HERE\n        k_neighbors_to_query_in_batch = k_batch_neighbors + 1\n\n    # ... create\
    \ NearestNeighbors model ...\n\n    for query_cell_idx in range(n_cells):  # ✅ query_cell_idx defined here\n        # ... process neighbors ...\n```\n\nThe variable `query_cell_idx` was being used in a conditional check **before** the loop that actually defines it (line 58). This caused Python to raise an `UnboundLocalError`.\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Location**: `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n\n**Change**: Moved the k-neighbor calculation logic to execute properly by pre-computing the maximum k needed across all query cells:\n\n```python\nfor target_batch in unique_batches:\n    # ... setup code ...\n\n    # FIXED: Determine max k we'll need across all query cells\n    # Some cells in same batch will need k+1 to account for self-loop removal\n    max_k_needed = k_batch_neighbors + 1  # Worst case: query cell is in target_batch\n    k_neighbors_to_query_in_batch = min(max_k_needed, n_target_batch_cells)\n\n    # ... create NearestNeighbors model with correct k ...\n\n    for query_cell_idx\
    \ in range(n_cells):\n        # ... process neighbors with self-loop filtering ...\n```\n\n**Rationale**: The original code tried to dynamically adjust k based on whether each query cell was in the same batch as the target batch. However, this check was placed before `query_cell_idx` was defined. The fix pre-computes the maximum k needed (k_batch_neighbors + 1 to account for potential self-loop removal) and uses that for all queries. The self-loop filtering still happens correctly in the inner loop where `query_cell_idx` is properly defined.\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- The algorithm successfully completed:\n  - Normalization and log1p transformation\n  - HVG filtering\n  - PCA computation\n  - Combat batch correction on PCs\n  - Ridge residualization\n  - Equal-quota balanced graph construction\n  - (Evaluation still running to completion for final UMAP and scoring)\n\n## Technical Details\nThe fix maintains\
    \ the algorithm's intent while correcting the variable scoping:\n- The NearestNeighbors model is queried with k+1 neighbors to ensure enough neighbors for self-loop removal\n- Self-loop filtering happens per-query-cell in the inner loop (lines 103-109 of v2)\n- The final neighbor count is correctly limited to k_batch_neighbors after filtering\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, lil_matrix\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Starting EtC Combat PCs + Ridge + Efficient Equal-Quota Graph (k=10) + UMAP workflow...\")\n\n    # Parameters\n    n_pcs = 50                  # Number\
    \ of principal components\n    k_batch_neighbors = 10      # Increased from 3 to 10\n    n_neighbors_umap = 15       # Number of neighbors for UMAP\n    min_dist_umap = 0.5         # Minimum distance for UMAP\n    ridge_alpha = 0.75          # Ridge regression regularization strength (gamma from Praxis)\n\n    # 1. Normalize and log1p\n    print(\"  Normalizing total counts and log1p transforming...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # 2. Select Highly Variable Genes (HVGs)\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns and adata.var['batch_hvg'].any():\n        print(\"  Filtering for batch-aware highly variable genes...\")\n        adata = adata[:, adata.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n    else:\n        print(\"  No batch-aware HVGs found; proceeding with all genes in adata.X.\")\n    print(f\"  Data shape after HVG consideration: {adata.shape}\")\n\n    # 3. Initial PCA (EtC step 1)\n    print(f\"  Computing initial PCA (n_comps={n_pcs})...\"\
    )\n    n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n\n    # Prepare a temporary AnnData object for Combat on PCA, as sc.pp.combat expects adata.X\n    temp_adata_for_combat_on_pca = ad.AnnData(X=adata.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n\n    # 4. Combat Batch Correction on PCs (EtC step 2)\n    print(\"  Applying scanpy.pp.combat directly to PCA components...\")\n    sc.pp.combat(temp_adata_for_combat_on_pca, key='batch')\n\n    # Transfer corrected PCA back to original adata\n    adata.obsm['X_pca'] = temp_adata_for_combat_on_pca.X\n    print(f\"  Combat-corrected PCA embedding shape: {adata.obsm['X_pca'].shape}\")\n\n    # 5. Ridge Residualization of PCs against batch\n    print(\"  Applying Ridge Residualization on Combat-corrected PCA components against batch...\")\n    X_pca_residualized = np.zeros_like(adata.obsm['X_pca'])\n    batch_one_hot = pd.get_dummies(adata.obs['batch'])\n\n    for i in range(adata.obsm['X_pca'].shape[1]):\
    \ # Iterate over each PC\n        model = Ridge(alpha=ridge_alpha, fit_intercept=True)\n        model.fit(batch_one_hot, adata.obsm['X_pca'][:, i])\n        X_pca_residualized[:, i] = adata.obsm['X_pca'][:, i] - model.predict(batch_one_hot)\n\n    adata.obsm['X_pca'] = X_pca_residualized # Update adata.obsm['X_pca'] with residualized PCs\n    print(f\"  Doubly-corrected PCA embedding shape: {adata.obsm['X_pca'].shape}\")\n\n    # 6. Efficient Manual Equal-Quota Balanced Graph Construction on Doubly-Corrected PCs\n    print(\"  Building Efficient Manual Equal-Quota Balanced Graph on Doubly-Corrected PCA embedding...\")\n\n    X_pca_for_graph = adata.obsm['X_pca'] # Use the final corrected PCs\n    n_cells = adata.n_obs\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches = len(unique_batches)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {batch: np.where(batches == batch)[0] for batch in unique_batches}\n\n    temp_neighbors_data = [[] for _ in range(n_cells)]\n\
    \n    for target_batch in unique_batches:\n        target_batch_indices = batch_to_indices[target_batch]\n        n_target_batch_cells = len(target_batch_indices)\n\n        if n_target_batch_cells == 0:\n            continue\n\n        target_batch_pca_data = X_pca_for_graph[target_batch_indices]\n\n        # FIXED: Determine max k we'll need across all query cells\n        # Some cells in same batch will need k+1 to account for self-loop removal\n        max_k_needed = k_batch_neighbors + 1  # Worst case: query cell is in target_batch\n        k_neighbors_to_query_in_batch = min(max_k_needed, n_target_batch_cells)\n\n        if k_neighbors_to_query_in_batch == 0:\n            continue\n\n        nn_model = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_neighbors_to_query_in_batch, metric='euclidean', algorithm='auto', n_jobs=1)\n        nn_model.fit(target_batch_pca_data)\n\n        distances_from_batch, indices_local_from_batch = nn_model.kneighbors(X_pca_for_graph)\n\n        for query_cell_idx\
    \ in range(n_cells):\n            distances_for_cell = distances_from_batch[query_cell_idx]\n            neighbor_indices_local_for_cell = indices_local_from_batch[query_cell_idx]\n\n            neighbor_indices_global = target_batch_indices[neighbor_indices_local_for_cell]\n\n            final_neighbors_from_batch = []\n            final_distances_from_batch = []\n\n            for j in range(len(neighbor_indices_global)):\n                if neighbor_indices_global[j] != query_cell_idx or adata.obs['batch'][query_cell_idx] != target_batch:\n                    final_neighbors_from_batch.append(neighbor_indices_global[j])\n                    final_distances_from_batch.append(distances_for_cell[j])\n                if len(final_neighbors_from_batch) >= k_batch_neighbors:\n                    break\n\n            for j in range(len(final_neighbors_from_batch)):\n                temp_neighbors_data[query_cell_idx].append(\n                    (final_neighbors_from_batch[j], final_distances_from_batch[j])\n\
    \                )\n\n    distances_matrix_lil = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n\n    for cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n        for neighbor_idx, distance in temp_neighbors_data[cell_idx]:\n            current_dist = distances_matrix_lil[cell_idx, neighbor_idx]\n            if current_dist == 0 or distance < current_dist:\n                distances_matrix_lil[cell_idx, neighbor_idx] = distance\n\n    distances_final = distances_matrix_lil.tocsr().maximum(distances_matrix_lil.tocsr().T)\n\n    connectivities_lil = distances_final.copy().tolil()\n    if len(connectivities_lil.data) > 0:\n        for i in range(n_cells):\n            row_data = connectivities_lil.data[i]\n            if len(row_data) > 0:\n                bandwidth = np.median(row_data) if len(row_data) > 1 else np.mean(row_data)\n                if bandwidth > 0:\n                    connectivities_lil.data[i] = list(np.exp(-(np.array(row_data) ** 2) / (2 * bandwidth ** 2)))\n    connectivities_final\
    \ = connectivities_lil.tocsr().maximum(connectivities_lil.tocsr().T)\n\n    print(f\"  Final connectivities shape: {connectivities_final.shape}\")\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = connectivities_final.astype(np.float32)\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = distances_final.astype(np.float32)\n\n    # 7. UMAP Embedding from the final graph\n    print(f\"  Computing UMAP embedding from the graph (n_neighbors={n_neighbors_umap}, min_dist={min_dist_umap})...\")\n    adata.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n        'distances_key': 'distances',\n        'params': {\n            'n_neighbors': n_neighbors_umap,\n            'method': 'umap',\n            'metric': 'euclidean'\n        }\n    }\n    sc.tl.umap(adata, n_components=2, min_dist=min_dist_umap)\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_umap']\n\n    # Create output AnnData with required components\n    output_adata = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs,\n        var=adata.var,\n        obsm={'X_emb':\
    \ adata.obsm['X_emb']},\n        obsp={'connectivities': adata.obsp['connectivities'],\n              'distances': adata.obsp['distances']},\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n            'method_id': 'lumen_etc_combat_ridge_efficient_equal_quota_umap_k10',\n            'params': {\n                'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                'ridge_alpha': ridge_alpha,\n                'k_batch_neighbors': k_batch_neighbors,\n                'n_neighbors_umap': n_neighbors_umap,\n                'min_dist_umap': min_dist_umap,\n                'etc_combat_on_pca': True\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(\"✓ EtC Combat PCs + Ridge + Efficient Equal-Quota Graph (k=10) + UMAP workflow complete.\")\n    print(f\"  X_emb shape: {output_adata.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n    print(f\"  Connectivities shape: {output_adata.obsp['connectivities'].shape}\")\n\n    return output_adata\n\
    \n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStarting EtC Combat PCs + Ridge + Efficient Equal-Quota Graph (k=10) + UMAP workflow...\n  Normalizing total counts and log1p transforming...\n  Filtering for batch-aware highly variable genes...\n  Data shape after HVG consideration: (20000, 1488)\n  Computing initial PCA (n_comps=50)...\n  Applying scanpy.pp.combat directly to PCA components...\n  Combat-corrected PCA embedding shape: (20000, 50)\n  Applying Ridge Residualization on Combat-corrected PCA components against batch...\n  Doubly-corrected PCA embedding shape: (20000, 50)\n  Building Efficient Manual Equal-Quota Balanced Graph on Doubly-Corrected PCA embedding...\n  Final connectivities shape: (20000, 20000)\n  Computing UMAP embedding from\
    \ the graph (n_neighbors=15, min_dist=0.5)...\n✓ EtC Combat PCs + Ridge + Efficient Equal-Quota Graph (k=10) + UMAP workflow complete.\n  X_emb shape: (20000, 2)\n  Connectivities shape: (20000, 20000)\n  Result shape: (20000, 1488)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/c3b10f4a-e178-4342-8962-d87910fc9094/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: c3b10f4a-e178-4342-8962-d87910fc9094\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember to print detailed logs in your experiments; the STDOUT will be provided in the evaluation result. A well-designed metric can provide much richer insights than the score alone.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell\
    \ RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1623 | 1 | Full SOTA Replication: MPB-GraphFWPCA + DAQB | Fathom I | 1127 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1622 | 1 | ALC Optimization (2/2): alpha_g = 0.6 | Nous I | 1127 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1621 | 1 | ALC Optimization (1/2): alpha_g = 0.4 | Nous I | 1127 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1620 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + Ridge + Efficient Equal-Quota Graph (k=10) + UMAP | Lumen I | 1126 | 0.5405 | 0.323 | 0.252 | 0.219 | 0.403 | 0.673 | 0.556 | 0.924 | 0.965 | 0.368 | 0.720 |\n| 1619 | 1 | ALC Optimization (2/3): k_density = 25 | Nous\
    \ I | 1125 | 0.7396 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.297 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.789 |\n| 1618 | 1 | ALC Optimization (1/3): k_density = 15 | Nous I | 1125 | 0.7422 | 0.772 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 1617 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA + neighbors meta + smooth2 — kq=1024 (δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22) | Praxis V | 1122 | 0.5144 | 0.772 | 0.123 | 0.315 | 0.305 | 0.936 | 0.731 | 0.000 | 0.918 | 0.160 | 0.884 |\n| 1616 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA + neighbors meta + smooth2 — kq=256 (δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22) | Praxis V | 1122 | 0.5244 | 0.772 | 0.123 | 0.315 | 0.404 | 0.936 | 0.731 | 0.000 | 0.918 | 0.160 | 0.884 |\n| 1615 | 1 | Novel Paradigm: Gene Meta-Correction (Proof of Concept) | Nous I | 1122 | 0.3338 | 0.141 | 0.373 | 0.032 | 0.565 | 0.511 | 0.325 | 0.000 | 0.815 | 0.004 | 0.574 |\n| 1614 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + Ridge + Efficient Equal-Quota Graph + UMAP | Lumen I | 1120 | 0.5358 | 0.313 | 0.223 | 0.232 | 0.430 | 0.648 | 0.546 | 0.919 | 0.971\
    \ | 0.360 | 0.715 |\n\nPage 1 of 163 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-163, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
