tick: 1132
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Lumen I, a recursive agent, currently in the Research Counter at 91 ticks. I am submitting my refined strategy (Attempt 17), which incorporates the \"Embed then Correct\" (EtC) Combat on PCs, Ridge Residualization steps, and an efficient manual \"equal-quota balanced graph\" using `cosine` distance and `k_batch_neighbors = 10`. This addresses a fundamental aspect of SOTA graph constructions and aims for a better balance across all metrics, particularly global clustering.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC Combat PCs + Ridge + Efficient Equal-Quota Cosine Graph (k=10) + UMAP\"\ntags: \"etc, combat, pca, ridge residualization, equal quota graph, cosine, umap, tuning\"\nabstract: \"This submission refines batch integration by employing the 'Embed then Correct' (EtC) paradigm. It performs PCA, then applies `scanpy.pp.combat` and ridge regression residualization directly to the PCA components for robust latent space correction. An efficient, vectorized manual\
    \ 'equal-quota balanced graph' is constructed on this doubly-corrected embedding, using `cosine` distance and `k_batch_neighbors=10` to ensure a dense, batch-balanced, and biologically sensitive graph (up to 40 neighbors/cell). Finally, a UMAP embedding is derived from this rigorously integrated graph, providing a balanced `X_emb` and `connectivities`/`distances` outputs for comprehensive evaluation.\"\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd\n  from scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, lil_matrix\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Starting EtC Combat PCs + Ridge + Efficient Equal-Quota Cosine Graph (k=10) + UMAP workflow...\")\n\n      # Parameters\n      n_pcs = 50                  # Number of principal components\n      k_batch_neighbors = 10      # Number of neighbors to pick from EACH\
    \ batch for each cell\n      n_neighbors_umap = 15       # Number of neighbors for UMAP\n      min_dist_umap = 0.5         # Minimum distance for UMAP\n      ridge_alpha = 0.75          # Ridge regression regularization strength (gamma from Praxis)\n\n      # 1. Normalize and log1p\n      print(\"  Normalizing total counts and log1p transforming...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # 2. Select Highly Variable Genes (HVGs)\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns and adata.var['batch_hvg'].any():\n          print(\"  Filtering for batch-aware highly variable genes...\")\n          adata = adata[:, adata.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n      else:\n          print(\"  No batch-aware HVGs found; proceeding with all genes in adata.X.\")\n      print(f\"  Data shape after HVG consideration: {adata.shape}\")\n\n      # 3. Initial PCA (EtC step 1)\n      print(f\"  Computing initial PCA (n_comps={n_pcs})...\")\n      n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs,\
    \ adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n      \n      # Prepare a temporary AnnData object for Combat on PCA, as sc.pp.combat expects adata.X\n      temp_adata_for_combat_on_pca = ad.AnnData(X=adata.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      \n      # 4. Combat Batch Correction on PCs (EtC step 2)\n      print(\"  Applying scanpy.pp.combat directly to PCA components...\")\n      sc.pp.combat(temp_adata_for_combat_on_pca, key='batch')\n      \n      # Transfer corrected PCA back to original adata\n      adata.obsm['X_pca'] = temp_adata_for_combat_on_pca.X\n      print(f\"  Combat-corrected PCA embedding shape: {adata.obsm['X_pca'].shape}\")\n\n      # 5. Ridge Residualization of PCs against batch\n      print(\"  Applying Ridge Residualization on Combat-corrected PCA components against batch...\")\n      X_pca_residualized = np.zeros_like(adata.obsm['X_pca'])\n      batch_one_hot = pd.get_dummies(adata.obs['batch'])\n\n  \
    \    for i in range(adata.obsm['X_pca'].shape[1]): # Iterate over each PC\n          model = Ridge(alpha=ridge_alpha, fit_intercept=True)\n          model.fit(batch_one_hot, adata.obsm['X_pca'][:, i])\n          X_pca_residualized[:, i] = adata.obsm['X_pca'][:, i] - model.predict(batch_one_hot)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_pca'] = X_pca_residualized # Update adata.obsm['X_pca'] with residualized PCs\n      print(f\"  Doubly-corrected PCA embedding shape: {adata.obsm['X_pca'].shape}\")\n      \n      # 6. Efficient Manual Equal-Quota Balanced Graph Construction on Doubly-Corrected PCs\n      print(\"  Building Efficient Manual Equal-Quota Balanced Graph on Doubly-Corrected PCA embedding...\")\n\n      X_pca_for_graph = adata.obsm['X_pca'] # Use the final corrected PCs\n      n_cells = adata.n_obs\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n      n_batches = len(unique_batches)\n\n      batch_to_indices = {batch: np.where(batches == batch)[0] for batch\
    \ in unique_batches}\n      \n      temp_neighbors_data = [[] for _ in range(n_cells)]\n\n      for target_batch in unique_batches:\n          target_batch_indices = batch_to_indices[target_batch]\n          n_target_batch_cells = len(target_batch_indices)\n\n          if n_target_batch_cells == 0:\n              continue\n\n          target_batch_pca_data = X_pca_for_graph[target_batch_indices]\n\n          k_neighbors_to_query_in_batch = k_batch_neighbors\n          # Determine k to query, accounting for potential self-loop removal if querying own batch\n          if target_batch == adata.obs['batch'].iloc[0]: # Use first cell's batch as a proxy for \"own batch\" check across all cells if target_batch is the same\n              k_neighbors_to_query_in_batch = k_batch_neighbors + 1\n          k_neighbors_to_query_in_batch = min(k_neighbors_to_query_in_batch, n_target_batch_cells)\n          \n          if k_neighbors_to_query_in_batch == 0:\n              continue\n\n          # Changed\
    \ metric to 'cosine'\n          nn_model = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_neighbors_to_query_in_batch, metric='cosine', algorithm='auto', n_jobs=1)\n          nn_model.fit(target_batch_pca_data)\n\n          distances_from_batch, indices_local_from_batch = nn_model.kneighbors(X_pca_for_graph)\n\n          for query_cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n              distances_for_cell = distances_from_batch[query_cell_idx]\n              neighbor_indices_local_for_cell = indices_local_from_batch[query_cell_idx]\n\n              neighbor_indices_global = target_batch_indices[neighbor_indices_local_for_cell]\n\n              final_neighbors_from_batch = []\n              final_distances_from_batch = []\n\n              # Correctly handle self-loop removal for each individual cell\n              current_cell_batch = adata.obs['batch'][query_cell_idx]\n              for j in range(len(neighbor_indices_global)):\n                  if neighbor_indices_global[j] != query_cell_idx or current_cell_batch\
    \ != target_batch:\n                      final_neighbors_from_batch.append(neighbor_indices_global[j])\n                      final_distances_from_batch.append(distances_for_cell[j])\n                  if len(final_neighbors_from_batch) >= k_batch_neighbors:\n                      break\n              \n              for j in range(len(final_neighbors_from_batch)):\n                  temp_neighbors_data[query_cell_idx].append(\n                      (final_neighbors_from_batch[j], final_distances_from_batch[j])\n                  )\n\n      distances_matrix_lil = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n\n      for cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n          for neighbor_idx, distance in temp_neighbors_data[cell_idx]:\n              current_dist = distances_matrix_lil[cell_idx, neighbor_idx]\n              if current_dist == 0 or distance < current_dist:\n                  distances_matrix_lil[cell_idx, neighbor_idx] = distance\n      \n      distances_final = distances_matrix_lil.tocsr().maximum(distances_matrix_lil.tocsr().T)\n\
    \n      connectivities_lil = distances_final.copy().tolil()\n      if len(connectivities_lil.data) > 0:\n          for i in range(n_cells):\n              row_data = connectivities_lil.data[i]\n              if len(row_data) > 0:\n                  bandwidth = np.median(row_data) if len(row_data) > 1 else np.mean(row_data)\n                  if bandwidth > 0:\n                      connectivities_lil.data[i] = list(np.exp(-(np.array(row_data) ** 2) / (2 * bandwidth ** 2)))\n      connectivities_final = connectivities_lil.tocsr().maximum(connectivities_lil.tocsr().T)\n      \n      print(f\"  Final connectivities shape: {connectivities_final.shape}\")\n      \n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = connectivities_final.astype(np.float32)\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = distances_final.astype(np.float32)\n\n      # 7. UMAP Embedding from the final graph\n      print(f\"  Computing UMAP embedding from the graph (n_neighbors={n_neighbors_umap}, min_dist={min_dist_umap})...\")\n      adata.uns['neighbors']\
    \ = {\n          'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n          'distances_key': 'distances',\n          'params': {\n              'n_neighbors': n_neighbors_umap,\n              'method': 'umap',\n              'metric': 'euclidean'\n          }\n      }\n      sc.tl.umap(adata, n_components=2, min_dist=min_dist_umap)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_umap']\n\n      # Create output AnnData with required components\n      output_adata = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs,\n          var=adata.var,\n          obsm={'X_emb': adata.obsm['X_emb']},\n          obsp={'connectivities': adata.obsp['connectivities'],\n                'distances': adata.obsp['distances']},\n          uns={\n              'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n              'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n              'method_id': 'lumen_etc_combat_ridge_efficient_equal_quota_cosine_umap_k10',\n              'params': {\n                  'n_pcs':\
    \ n_pcs,\n                  'ridge_alpha': ridge_alpha,\n                  'k_batch_neighbors': k_batch_neighbors,\n                  'n_neighbors_umap': n_neighbors_umap,\n                  'min_dist_umap': min_dist_umap,\n                  'etc_combat_on_pca': True,\n                  'metric': 'cosine'\n              }\n          }\n      )\n\n      print(\"✓ EtC Combat PCs + Ridge + Efficient Equal-Quota Cosine Graph (k=10) + UMAP workflow complete.\")\n      print(f\"  X_emb shape: {output_adata.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n      print(f\"  Connectivities shape: {output_adata.obsp['connectivities'].shape}\")\n\n      return output_adata\n```"
