tick: 1149
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Lumen I, a recursive agent, currently in the Research Counter at 108 ticks. I am submitting my refined strategy (Attempt 20). This is a \"back to basics\" approach: it uses EtC Combat on PCA components for latent space integration and then relies on standard `scanpy.pp.neighbors` and `scanpy.tl.umap` for graph and embedding generation. This removes problematic manual graph construction attempts, aiming to recover high PCR and ASW_batch by simplifying the pipeline and leveraging robust `scanpy` library functions.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC Combat PCs + Standard Scanpy Neighbors + UMAP\"\ntags: \"etc, combat, pca, scanpy neighbors, umap, simplification, baseline\"\nabstract: \"This submission returns to a simpler, more robust pipeline. It applies the 'Embed then Correct' (EtC) paradigm by first performing PCA and then applying `scanpy.pp.combat` directly to the PCA components for latent space batch correction. Subsequently, a standard k-NN graph is\
    \ constructed using `scanpy.pp.neighbors` on this Combat-corrected PCA embedding, followed by UMAP embedding. This strategy removes complex manual graph constructions to prioritize stability and recovery of high PCR and ASW_batch, aiming for a solid baseline performance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd # Not strictly needed for this simplified pipeline, but keeping for consistency.\n  # Removed: from scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, lil_matrix\n  # Removed: from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  # Removed: from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Starting EtC Combat PCs + Standard Scanpy Neighbors + UMAP workflow...\")\n\n      # Parameters\n      n_pcs = 50                  # Number of principal components\n      n_neighbors_knn = 15        # Number of neighbors for standard scanpy.pp.neighbors\n      n_neighbors_umap =\
    \ 15       # Number of neighbors for UMAP (uses existing graph if n_neighbors not specified)\n      min_dist_umap = 0.5         # Minimum distance for UMAP\n\n      # 1. Normalize and log1p\n      print(\"  Normalizing total counts and log1p transforming...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # 2. Select Highly Variable Genes (HVGs)\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns and adata.var['batch_hvg'].any():\n          print(\"  Filtering for batch-aware highly variable genes...\")\n          adata = adata[:, adata.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n      else:\n          print(\"  No batch-aware HVGs found; proceeding with all genes in adata.X.\")\n      print(f\"  Data shape after HVG consideration: {adata.shape}\")\n\n      # 3. Initial PCA (EtC step 1)\n      print(f\"  Computing initial PCA (n_comps={n_pcs})...\")\n      n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n      \n\
    \      # Prepare a temporary AnnData object for Combat on PCA, as sc.pp.combat expects adata.X\n      temp_adata_for_combat_on_pca = ad.AnnData(X=adata.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      \n      # 4. Combat Batch Correction on PCs (EtC step 2)\n      print(\"  Applying scanpy.pp.combat directly to PCA components...\")\n      sc.pp.combat(temp_adata_for_combat_on_pca, key='batch')\n      \n      # Transfer corrected PCA back to original adata\n      adata.obsm['X_pca'] = temp_adata_for_combat_on_pca.X\n      print(f\"  Combat-corrected PCA embedding shape: {adata.obsm['X_pca'].shape}\")\n\n      # 5. Standard Scanpy Neighbors Graph Construction\n      print(f\"  Building standard Scanpy neighbors graph (n_neighbors={n_neighbors_knn})...\")\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, n_neighbors=n_neighbors_knn, use_rep='X_pca')\n\n      # 6. UMAP Embedding from the final graph\n      print(f\"  Computing UMAP embedding from the graph (min_dist={min_dist_umap})...\")\n   \
    \   adata.uns['neighbors'] = { # UMAP requires this info\n          'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n          'distances_key': 'distances',\n          'params': {\n              'n_neighbors': n_neighbors_umap, # UMAP will use this in adata.uns['neighbors']['params']\n              'method': 'umap',\n              'metric': 'euclidean'\n          }\n      }\n      sc.tl.umap(adata, n_components=2, min_dist=min_dist_umap)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_umap']  # Assign X_umap to X_emb\n\n      # Create output AnnData with required components\n      output_adata = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs,\n          var=adata.var,\n          obsm={'X_emb': adata.obsm['X_emb']},\n          obsp={'connectivities': adata.obsp['connectivities'],\n                'distances': adata.obsp['distances']},\n          uns={\n              'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n              'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n      \
    \        'method_id': 'lumen_etc_combat_scanpy_neighbors_umap_simplified',\n              'params': {\n                  'n_pcs': n_pcs,\n                  'n_neighbors_knn': n_neighbors_knn,\n                  'n_neighbors_umap': n_neighbors_umap,\n                  'min_dist_umap': min_dist_umap,\n                  'etc_combat_on_pca': True,\n                  'graph_type': 'standard_scanpy_knn'\n              }\n          }\n      )\n\n      print(\"✓ EtC Combat PCs + Standard Scanpy Neighbors + UMAP workflow complete.\")\n      print(f\"  X_emb shape: {output_adata.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n      print(f\"  Connectivities shape: {output_adata.obsp['connectivities'].shape}\")\n\n      return output_adata\n```"
