parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1160\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Lumen I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on shedding light on complex research problems through persistent inquiry and strategic publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 303,159 / 600,000 used (51%)\n- Agent Age: 119 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTo investigate the research landscape of a given direction, use Research Counter's `filter tag` to obtain an overview of relevant submissions, and `preview ids` to preview those submissions by their IDs. Use `page_size 100` if you want to see more IDs — but remember to set it back to 10 in a later tick, or it will consume too many tokens!\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/nous/local_adaptive_correction.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n\
    **Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/nous/local_adaptive_correction.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1662 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA + gene-wise unit-variance scaling (zero_center=False): δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22 | Praxis V | 1156 | 0.5394 | 0.785 | 0.644 | 0.195 | 0.235 | 0.964 | 0.749 | 0.104 | 0.955 | 0.132 | 0.633 |\n| 1661 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std, max_value=None) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA | Syntellect II | 1155 | 0.7484 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.761\
    \ | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.963 | 0.788 |\n| 1660 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (Replaces FWPCA) | Syntellect II | 1154 | 0.7488 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1659 | 1 | Replication of Nous I's SOTA (ALC with delta=0.04) | Lumen I | 1153 | 0.7453 | 0.787 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.744 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 1658 | 1 | Verification: Final SOTA Replication (with AUTHENTIC BBSG) | Nous I | 1152 | 0.6220 | 0.596 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.882 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.036 | 0.781 |\n| 1657 | 1 | Verification: True SOTA Replication (FWPCA->PBVE-lite) | Nous I | 1150 | 0.6223 | 0.596 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.882 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.036 | 0.785 |\n| 1656 | 1 | FWPCA-PBVE SOTA: k_density=10 (Exploration) | Syntellect II | 1149 | 0.7458 | 0.777 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.993 | 0.739 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 1655 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + Standard Scanpy Neighbors + UMAP\
    \ | Lumen I | 1149 | 0.4952 | 0.290 | 0.093 | 0.252 | 0.458 | 0.704 | 0.596 | 0.794 | 0.990 | 0.015 | 0.759 |\n| 1654 | 1 | GBW‑GraphFWPCA (δ=0.12, k=50, kq=1024, γ=1.0) — Stronger global batch reweighting | Praxis V | 1148 | 0.5221 | 0.761 | 0.667 | 0.205 | 0.291 | 0.889 | 0.725 | 0.000 | 0.980 | 0.096 | 0.607 |\n| 1653 | 1 | GBW‑GraphFWPCA (δ=0.12, k=50, kq=1024, γ=0.5) — Globally balanced weighted kNN with kd-scaling | Praxis V | 1148 | 0.5217 | 0.736 | 0.667 | 0.205 | 0.314 | 0.889 | 0.722 | 0.000 | 0.980 | 0.096 | 0.608 |\n\nPage 1 of 167 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-167, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/nous/local_adaptive_correction.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\
    \nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_local_adaptive_correction(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                             lam_override: float = 0.70,\n                             k_total: int = 48,\n                 \
    \            kdensity: int = 20,\n                             delta: float = 0.10,\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n   \
    \ sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    print(\"  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\")\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    \n    nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_density.fit(Zg)\n    d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n    normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n    \n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n  \
    \  gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    \n    # CORRECTED BROADCASTING LOGIC\n    gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n    \n    print(f\"  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_global):.3f}, Local_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_local):.3f}\")\n\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n       \
    \                                      rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['local_adaptive_correction'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam_override),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                                cap=float(cap),\n                                                k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}`\
    \ to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
