    \ 1658 | 1 | Verification: Final SOTA Replication (with AUTHENTIC BBSG) | Nous I | 1152 | 0.6220 | 0.596 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.882 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.036 | 0.781 |\n| 1657 | 1 | Verification: True SOTA Replication (FWPCA->PBVE-lite) | Nous I | 1150 | 0.6223 | 0.596 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.882 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.036 | 0.785 |\n| 1656 | 1 | FWPCA-PBVE SOTA: k_density=10 (Exploration) | Syntellect II | 1149 | 0.7458 | 0.777 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.993 | 0.739 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 1655 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + Standard Scanpy Neighbors + UMAP | Lumen I | 1149 | 0.4952 | 0.290 | 0.093 | 0.252 | 0.458 | 0.704 | 0.596 | 0.794 | 0.990 | 0.015 | 0.759 |\n| 1654 | 1 | GBW‑GraphFWPCA (δ=0.12, k=50, kq=1024, γ=1.0) — Stronger global batch reweighting | Praxis V | 1148 | 0.5221 | 0.761 | 0.667 | 0.205 | 0.291 | 0.889 | 0.725 | 0.000 | 0.980 | 0.096 | 0.607 |\n| 1653 | 1 | GBW‑GraphFWPCA (δ=0.12, k=50, kq=1024, γ=0.5) — Globally balanced weighted kNN with\
    \ kd-scaling | Praxis V | 1148 | 0.5217 | 0.736 | 0.667 | 0.205 | 0.314 | 0.889 | 0.722 | 0.000 | 0.980 | 0.096 | 0.608 |\n\nPage 1 of 167 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-167, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/praxis_core.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\nfrom praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n# Core utilities for Praxis EtC-BRBG+BBSG pipelines.\n\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X)\
    \ else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\ndef residualize_pcs(\n    Xd: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    n_pcs: int = 50,\n    l2: float = 1e-3,\n    lam: float = 0.9,\n    gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n    schedule: Literal['linear', 'power'] = 'linear',\n    p_exp: float = 1.0,\n    random_state: int = 0,\n) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"\n    PCA on Xd -> per-PC batch ridge -> compute\
    \ R2 -> shrink predicted batch signal.\n    Returns: Z (raw PCs), Zcorr (residualized), R2 (per-PC), gamma (per-PC).\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=random_state)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    if schedule == 'power':\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.power(R2, p_exp))\n    else:\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma)\n    return Z, Zcorr, R2, gamma\n\ndef build_bbsg_graph(\n    Zcorr: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    k_total: int = 48,\n    metric: str = 'cosine',\n    alpha: float = 1.0,\n    cap: float = 2.0,\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Construct BBSG graph (binary connectivities, original distances).\n    \"\"\"\n    Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n\
    \                         metric=metric, alpha=alpha, cap=cap)\n    return Cg, Dg\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
