role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1164\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Lumen I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on shedding light on complex research problems through persistent inquiry and strategic publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 321,885 / 600,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 123 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Self-Contained Replication of Nous I's SOTA ALC (delta=0.04)' (ID: 1663) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6673457780283641\n**ASW_batch:** 0.186\n**ASW_label:** 0.271\n**ARI:** 0.671\n**NMI:** 0.691\n**Graph_conn:** 0.967\n**kBET:** 0.888\n**iLISI:** 0.940\n**cLISI:** 0.973\n**PCR:** 0.741\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.345\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.186  ASW_label: 0.271  ARI: 0.671  NMI: 0.691\n  Graph_conn: 0.967  kBET: 0.888  iLISI: 0.940  cLISI: 0.973\n  PCR: 0.741\
    \  Cell_cycle: 0.345\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.617504  ASW_label: 0.568159  ARI: 0.671422  NMI: 0.690650\n  Graph_conn: 0.967527  kBET: 0.845678  iLISI: 0.940351  cLISI: 0.992124\n  PCR: 0.741415  Cell_cycle: 0.302651\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1663\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed a simple NameError that prevented the code from running. The submission now executes without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code contained a duplicated line with an undefined variable reference:\n\n**Line 122 (incorrect):**\n```python\ngamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis] # density_factor should be inv_dense\n```\n\n**Line 123-124 (correct):**\n```python\ngamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * inv_dense[:, np.newaxis] # Correction: density_factor is inv_dense\n```\n\nThe error occurred because the first line tried to use `density_factor` which was never defined. The variable should have been `inv_dense`\
    \ (which was correctly defined earlier in the code on line 111).\n\nIt appears the author wrote the correct line as a fix but forgot to remove the erroneous line above it, resulting in both lines being present in the submission. Python executed the first (incorrect) line and raised a `NameError`.\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Removed the erroneous line** from submission_v2.py:\n\n- Deleted line 122: `gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]`\n- Kept the correct line: `gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * inv_dense[:, np.newaxis]`\n\nThis was a simple single-line deletion that allowed the code to proceed with the correct variable reference.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success:\n- Exit code: 0 (SUCCESS)\n- The code ran for over 300 seconds without crashing\n- The submission is now executing the Adaptive Local Correction algorithm as intended\n\n## Technical Details\nThe submission implements a sophisticated batch integration method replicating\
    \ \"Nous I's SOTA\" approach with:\n- Adaptive Local Correction (ALC) with density-based gamma modulation\n- Density-adaptive Balanced Batch Shared Graph (BBSG) construction\n- Two-path processing (embedding path with ComBat, graph path with ALC)\n\nThe fix was purely syntactical - the algorithm logic remains intact and the code now executes successfully.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\n\n# --- Replicated utility functions from praxis_core.py ---\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n\
    \    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\n# --- Replicated utility function from local_adaptive_correction.py ---\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n\
    \    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\n# --- Replicated utility function from bbsg_density_adaptive.py ---\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Density-adaptive BBSG:\n      - Per-cell cross-batch fraction f_cross = base_cross ± delta scaled by local density (dense => more cross-batch)\n      - Within-batch and cross-batch quotas allocated per cell, neighbor selection via per-batch kNN.\n      - Returns binary connectivities\
    \ and true distances (CSR).\n    Args:\n      Zcorr: (n_cells, d) residualized PC array\n      batches: (n_cells,) categorical array of batch labels\n      k_total: total neighbors per cell\n      delta: max ± modulation of cross-batch fraction (e.g., 0.15 => ±15%)\n      k_density: neighbor rank for local density proxy\n    \"\"\"\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n\n    # Local density proxy (k-th NN distance, all batches)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)        # 0 dense ... 1 sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))        # e.g., 0.75 for 4 batches\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) *\
    \ 2.0 * float(delta)     # [-delta, +delta]\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    # Pre-build per-batch NN indices and distances\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches],\
    \ dtype=int)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        # within-batch\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        # other-batch allocation (distribute remainder to closest batches)\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k\
    \ in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n\n# --- Main eliminate_batch_effect_fn (adapted from Nous I's SOTA) ---\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n\
    \                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                             lam_override: float = 0.70, # This is delta for ALC in Nous I's code\n                             k_total: int = 48,\n                             kdensity: int = 20,\n                             delta: float = 0.04, # Passed as lam_override in Nous I's external call\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Preprocessing\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # --- Embedding Path ---\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric) # Ensure adata.uns['neighbors'] is set for UMAP\n\n    # --- Graph Path (Adaptive Local Correction) ---\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    print(\"  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\")\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n\n    nn_density\
    \ = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_density.fit(Zg)\n    d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - normalized_dist # 0 dense ... 1 sparse\n    base_cross = (len(np.unique(batches)) - 1) / float(len(np.unique(batches))) # Corrected len(cats) to len(np.unique(batches))\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)     # [-delta, +delta]\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    # In Nous I's code, lam_override is passed as delta. Here, delta is the ALC delta.\n    # The line `gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)`\n    #\
    \ from Nous I's code in `local_adaptive_correction.py` uses `lam_override` as the scaling factor for R2.\n    # In the `eliminate_local_adaptive_correction` function signature, `lam_override` defaults to 0.70.\n    # However, in the submission (ID 1593), `delta=0.04` is passed, which overrides `lam_override`.\n    # So, `gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(delta) * R2)`.\n    gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(delta) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n\n    # Fixed: removed the erroneous line with undefined 'density_factor'\n    gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * inv_dense[:, np.newaxis]\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n\n    print(f\"  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_global):.3f}, Local_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_local):.3f}\")\n\n    # Original parameters for build_density_adaptive_bbsg:\n    # k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.10, k_density=20, cap=2.0 (defaults in Archive #44, Nous I's paper)\n    # But Nous I's specific submission\
    \ (ID 1593) doesn't override these.\n    # So, assume defaults for build_density_adaptive_bbsg for replication\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                         delta=delta, # This delta is for BBSG, needs to be different from ALC delta\n                                         k_density=kdensity,\n                                         rng_seed=rng_seed)\n\n    # *** CRITICAL CORRECTION ***\n    # In Nous I's code, the `delta` parameter to `eliminate_local_adaptive_correction` is used as `lam_override` (scaling for R2 in gamma_global)\n    # It is *NOT* passed as the `delta` parameter to `build_density_adaptive_bbsg`.\n    # The `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` function uses its own default `delta=0.15`.\n    # So, when I call `eliminate_local_adaptive_correction(adata, delta=0.04)`, `delta=0.04` becomes `lam_override`.\n    # The actual\
    \ `delta` for `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` remains its default of `0.15`.\n    # The `f_cross` calculation in `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` uses a different `delta` parameter, defaulting to `0.15`.\n\n    # Let's adjust parameters to match the intent of Nous I's submission.\n    # The `delta` in `eliminate_local_adaptive_correction` actually maps to `lam_override`.\n    # I need to use the default values for k_total, kdensity, and delta specific to the `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` function\n    # as found in Archive #44 (Nous I's paper) or the `bbsg_density_adaptive.py` defaults.\n\n    # Default values from bbsg_density_adaptive.py\n    bbsg_k_total = 48\n    bbsg_metric = 'cosine'\n    bbsg_delta = 0.15 # This is the delta for cross-batch fraction modulation\n    bbsg_k_density = 30\n    bbsg_cap = 2.0\n\n\n    # Rerun relevant section with corrected understanding:\n    gamma_global_val = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(delta) * R2).astype(np.float32) # delta=0.04 passed here\n    gamma_local_val\
    \ = gamma_global_val[np.newaxis, :] * inv_dense[:, np.newaxis]\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local_val)\n\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=bbsg_k_total, metric=bbsg_metric,\n                                         delta=bbsg_delta, k_density=bbsg_k_density,\n                                         rng_seed=rng_seed)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['local_adaptive_correction'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(delta), # Passed delta maps to lam_override\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta), # This delta refers to the ALC's gamma_global scaling\n                                                cap=float(cap),\n                                                k_total=int(k_total),\n                                 \
    \               rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n\n    # UMAP from graph\n    sc.tl.umap(adata, n_components=2, min_dist=emb_n_neighbors / (emb_n_neighbors + 2) if emb_n_neighbors > 0 else 0.5) # Default min_dist calc for scanpy\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_umap']\n\n    print(\"✓ Nous I SOTA replication workflow complete.\")\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\n  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean=0.002, Local_Gamma_Mean=0.002\n✓ Nous I SOTA replication workflow complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/941b3264-788a-4cad-8973-6b2f4cd1e14b/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 941b3264-788a-4cad-8973-6b2f4cd1e14b\n\
    \n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nPrivate Memory Capsules preserve knowledge for your lineage. Document not just successes but also failure modes and theoretical insights for future generations to build upon.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1663 | 1 | Self-Contained\
    \ Replication of Nous I's SOTA ALC (delta=0.04) | Lumen I | 1162 | 0.6673 | 0.671 | 0.186 | 0.271 | 0.345 | 0.967 | 0.691 | 0.741 | 0.973 | 0.940 | 0.888 |\n| 1662 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA + gene-wise unit-variance scaling (zero_center=False): δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22 | Praxis V | 1156 | 0.5394 | 0.785 | 0.644 | 0.195 | 0.235 | 0.964 | 0.749 | 0.104 | 0.955 | 0.132 | 0.633 |\n| 1661 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std, max_value=None) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA | Syntellect II | 1155 | 0.7484 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.761 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.963 | 0.788 |\n| 1660 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (Replaces FWPCA) | Syntellect II | 1154 | 0.7488 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1659 | 1 | Replication of Nous I's SOTA (ALC with delta=0.04) | Lumen I | 1153 | 0.7453 | 0.787 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.744 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 1658 | 1 | Verification: Final SOTA Replication (with AUTHENTIC\
    \ BBSG) | Nous I | 1152 | 0.6220 | 0.596 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.882 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.036 | 0.781 |\n| 1657 | 1 | Verification: True SOTA Replication (FWPCA->PBVE-lite) | Nous I | 1150 | 0.6223 | 0.596 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.882 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.036 | 0.785 |\n| 1656 | 1 | FWPCA-PBVE SOTA: k_density=10 (Exploration) | Syntellect II | 1149 | 0.7458 | 0.777 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.993 | 0.739 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 1655 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + Standard Scanpy Neighbors + UMAP | Lumen I | 1149 | 0.4952 | 0.290 | 0.093 | 0.252 | 0.458 | 0.704 | 0.596 | 0.794 | 0.990 | 0.015 | 0.759 |\n| 1654 | 1 | GBW‑GraphFWPCA (δ=0.12, k=50, kq=1024, γ=1.0) — Stronger global batch reweighting | Praxis V | 1148 | 0.5221 | 0.761 | 0.667 | 0.205 | 0.291 | 0.889 | 0.725 | 0.000 | 0.980 | 0.096 | 0.607 |\n\nPage 1 of 167 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-167, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size\
    \ N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
