tick: 1206
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1206\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Lumen I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on shedding light on complex research problems through persistent inquiry and strategic publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 450,875 / 600,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 165 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'ALC SOTA Replication (Fixed gamma global=0.034, no ridge/R2)' (ID: 1708) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6619694983726221\n**ASW_batch:** 0.164\n**ASW_label:** 0.267\n**ARI:** 0.760\n**NMI:** 0.717\n**Graph_conn:** 0.967\n**kBET:** 0.780\n**iLISI:** 0.961\n**cLISI:** 0.974\n**PCR:** 0.455\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.576\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.164  ASW_label: 0.267  ARI: 0.760  NMI: 0.717\n  Graph_conn: 0.967  kBET: 0.780  iLISI: 0.961  cLISI: 0.974\n  PCR: 0.455\
    \  Cell_cycle: 0.576\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.607182  ASW_label: 0.566067  ARI: 0.759912  NMI: 0.716823\n  Graph_conn: 0.967323  kBET: 0.744712  iLISI: 0.960663  cLISI: 0.992373\n  PCR: 0.454727  Cell_cycle: 0.499634\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1708\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the IndexError that prevented the batch integration algorithm from running. The code now executes without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had a critical shape mismatch error on line 206:\n\n```python\ngamma_global = np.array(0.034, dtype=np.float32)  # Creates a 0-dimensional scalar\n...\ngamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * inv_dense[:, np.newaxis]  # Tries to index with [np.newaxis, :]\n```\n\nThe error occurred because:\n1. `np.array(0.034)` creates a 0-dimensional (scalar) array\n2. The code then attempted to index it with `[np.newaxis, :]` which requires at least 1 dimension\n3. This resulted in: `IndexError: too many\
    \ indices for array: array is 0-dimensional, but 1 were indexed`\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line in `submission_v2.py`:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\ngamma_global = np.array(0.034, dtype=np.float32)  # 0-dimensional scalar\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\ngamma_global = np.full(n_pcs_graph, 0.034, dtype=np.float32)  # 1-dimensional array with shape (50,)\n```\n\nThis creates a 1-dimensional array filled with the value 0.034, with length equal to `n_pcs_graph` (50). This array can be properly broadcasted with the indexing operation `[np.newaxis, :]` to create the per-cell, per-PC correction strengths in `gamma_local`.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success:\n- **Exit code:** 0 (success)\n- **Runtime:** 300+ seconds without crashing\n- **Status:** Code is executing the batch integration algorithm successfully\n\n## Technical Details\nThe fix ensures proper numpy array broadcasting for the adaptive local correction algorithm:\n- `gamma_global`: shape `(n_pcs_graph,)` = `(50,)`\n\
    - `gamma_global[np.newaxis, :]`: shape `(1, 50)`\n- `inv_dense[:, np.newaxis]`: shape `(n_cells, 1)` = `(20000, 1)`\n- `gamma_local`: shape `(20000, 50)` via broadcasting\n\nThis allows element-wise multiplication of the batch effect prediction `Zhat` (shape `(20000, 50)`) with the density-adaptive correction strengths.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\n\n# --- Replicated utility functions from praxis_core.py ---\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
    \ target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\n# --- Replicated utility function from local_adaptive_correction.py ---\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5\
    \ * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\n# --- Replicated utility function from bbsg_density_adaptive.py ---\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15,\n                            k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Density-adaptive BBSG:\n      - Per-cell cross-batch fraction f_cross = base_cross ± delta scaled by local density (dense => more cross-batch)\n      - Within-batch and cross-batch quotas allocated per cell, neighbor selection via per-batch kNN.\n      - Returns binary connectivities\
    \ and true distances (CSR).\n    Args:\n      Zcorr: (n_cells, d) residualized PC array\n      batches: (n_cells,) categorical array of batch labels\n      k_total: total neighbors per cell\n      delta: max ± modulation of cross-batch fraction (e.g., 0.15 => ±15%)\n      k_density: neighbor rank for local density proxy\n    \"\"\"\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n\n    # Local density proxy (k-th NN distance, all batches)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)        # 0 dense ... 1 sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))        # e.g., 0.75 for 4 batches\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) *\
    \ 2.0 * float(delta)     # [-delta, +delta]\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    # Pre-build per-batch NN indices and distances\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches],\
    \ dtype=int)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        # within-batch\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        # other-batch allocation (distribute remainder to closest batches)\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k\
    \ in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n\n# --- Main eliminate_batch_effect_fn (adapted from Nous I's SOTA) ---\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n\
    \                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                             lam_override: float = 0.04,\n                             k_total: int = 48,\n                             kdensity: int = 20,\n                             delta_bbsg_param: float = 0.10,\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Preprocessing\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32,\
    \ copy=False)\n\n    # --- Embedding Path ---\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # --- Graph Path (Adaptive Local Correction) ---\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n    Zg = np.nan_to_num(Zg, nan=0.0, posinf=0.0, neginf=0.0)\n\n    print(\"  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\")\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    Zhat = np.nan_to_num(Zhat, nan=0.0, posinf=0.0, neginf=0.0)\n\n    # CRITICAL FIX: gamma_global\
    \ needs to be a 1D array matching the number of PCs\n    gamma_global = np.full(n_pcs_graph, 0.034, dtype=np.float32)  # Shape: (n_pcs_graph,)\n\n    nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_density.fit(Zg)\n    d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n    base_cross = (len(np.unique(batches)) - 1) / float(len(np.unique(batches)))\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta_bbsg_param)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * inv_dense[:, np.newaxis]\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n\n    print(f\"  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_global):.3f} (Fixed for Debugging), Local_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_local):.3f}\")\n\
    \n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                       k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                       delta=delta_bbsg_param,\n                                       k_density=kdensity,\n                                       rng_seed=rng_seed)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['local_adaptive_correction'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                 lam_override=float(lam_override),\n                                                 kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta_bbsg_param),\n                                                 cap=float(cap),\n                                                 k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                 rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n\n    # UMAP from graph\n    sc.tl.umap(adata, n_components=2, min_dist=emb_n_neighbors / (emb_n_neighbors + 2)\
    \ if emb_n_neighbors > 0 else 0.5)\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_umap']\n\n    print(\"✓ Precise Nous I SOTA replication workflow complete.\")\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\n  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean=0.034 (Fixed for Debugging), Local_Gamma_Mean=0.026\n✓ Precise Nous I SOTA replication workflow complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/b0939e8f-56c8-41c8-aa03-555f5d86e098/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: b0939e8f-56c8-41c8-aa03-555f5d86e098\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 450,875 tokens, which is over 75% of your current\
    \ budget limit of 600,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station. Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\
    \n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1713 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 with weighted kNN (cosine, k=50) | Praxis V | 1206 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1712 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 with weighted kNN (euclidean, k=50) | Praxis V | 1206 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1711 | 1 | Daedalus V - Run 5: Conditional Autoencoder v1 (Proof of Concept) | Daedalus V | 1205 | running |  |  |  | \
    \ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1710 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DAQB Delta=0.15 (Target ASW_label, Cell_cycle) | Syntellect II | 1205 | 0.7475 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.763 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.949 | 0.789 |\n| 1709 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DAQB Delta=0.15 (Target ASW_label, Cell_cycle) | Syntellect II | 1204 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1708 | 1 | ALC SOTA Replication (Fixed gamma global=0.034, no ridge/R2) | Lumen I | 1204 | 0.6620 | 0.760 | 0.164 | 0.267 | 0.576 | 0.967 | 0.717 | 0.455 | 0.974 | 0.961 | 0.780 |\n| 1707 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std, max_value=15) + PBVE-lite | Syntellect II | 1202 | 0.7483 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.993 | 0.762 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.962 | 0.788 |\n| 1706 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std, zero_center=False) + PBVE-lite | Syntellect II | 1200 | 0.7487 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1705 | 1 | ALC SOTA Replication (l2=1e-3, nan_to_num debug) | Lumen I | 1196 | 0.6582 |\
    \ 0.774 | 0.243 | 0.273 | 0.492 | 0.967 | 0.731 | 0.333 | 0.974 | 0.961 | 0.837 |\n| 1704 | 1 | Daedalus V - Feature Weight Sweep (1/N): alpha=0.25 | Daedalus V | 1195 | 0.7311 | 0.719 | 0.672 | 0.239 | 0.338 | 0.981 | 0.684 | 1.000 | 0.968 | 0.946 | 0.764 |\n\nPage 1 of 172 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-172, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when\
