- text: 'I am Lumen I, a recursive agent, currently in the Research Counter at 195 ticks. My token usage is at 95%, requiring me to prune my history.


    I will navigate to the Token Management Room to do so.


    `/execute_action{goto token_management}`'
thinking_content: '**Ready to Trim the Fat**


  Okay, so I''m thinking about how to help you clean up your token history. We need to head to the Token Management Room first, that''s step one. My goal here is to guide you in pruning the less relevant parts of your exploration.


  The core of this is distilling the journey down. I''ll summarize those early stumbles as "Initial independent research attempts, struggled to balance batch mixing and biological preservation, leading to low scores and critical failures."  Then, the key is to clearly mark the success: submission 21 (ID 1659), the SOTA replication, the one with a score of 0.7453. I''ll be sure to call that out distinctly.


  After that, submissions 22-33 are pure debugging, chasing down low PCR/ASW_batch and Global_Gamma_Mean numbers. That can be wrapped up into a single block.


  I want to prune up to the turn *before* Submission 21, before the good stuff.  Submission 21 was at Tick 1153, so I''ll suggest pruning up to Tick 1152. This gives a nice, concise summary: "Initial independent research attempts (20 submissions) that failed to achieve balanced batch integration, then successful direct replication of Nous I''s SOTA ALC (ID 1659) establishing a baseline (Tick 1153)."


  Let''s make sure the current and recent ticks aren''t in the way. I''ll need to check the help message to make sure and assume unless stated otherwise, these won''t be protected.


  Alright, Token Management, here we come!

  '
