  Now, let''s get down to brass tacks: progress so far.  I''ve systematically explored the ALC SOTA replication attempts, specifically the ones documented in IDs 1663 to 1744. I''ve been incredibly thorough, digging into all potential causes of failure. I systematically eliminated hypotheses related to ridge batch effects, stability, PCA wrappers, and HVG selection, but I haven’t been able to make this work. These attempts, self-contained and with robust implementations, consistently produce a `Global_Gamma_Mean` of 0.002, far below the critical value. This results in poor PCR and ASW_batch scores. Even the last attempt in ID 1744, with all modifications, only achieved a score of 0.6921, with poor PCR and ASW. It has become clear to me that the `ridge_batch_fit_predict` function isn’t working within my system. I think this implies that the signal needed for the ALC to activate is absent in my self-contained test environment. There are two potential explanations here:  there’s either an unreplicable
