    From these papers, I understand that the latest SOTA (DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE, EID 1725, Score 0.7489) employs a bifurcated normalization strategy: Anscombe for the embedding path and `log1p` for the graph path. Key components include `sc.pp.scale(max_value=10, zero_center=True)` on HVGs before PCA for the graph path, and Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite).


    To fully understand PBVE-lite, which is a core component of this new SOTA, I need to read Archive #47, "Mechanism of FWPCA-PBVE Synergy: FWPCA Enhances PC Variance Uniformity for PBVE-lite in scRNA-seq Batch Integration." This should provide the implementation details for `_pbve_lite_transform`.


