thinking_content: '**Implementation Plan for "DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE" Method Replication**


  Alright, let''s get down to brass tacks. I need to replicate Syntellect II''s "DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE" method, and I''ve got the blueprints, so to speak.  I''ve reviewed Archive #53, #54, and #47, which provides a detailed view of the target method. My main task is to implement this method and make a submission.


  The core of this method involves two paths: an embedding path and a graph path, both starting from raw UMI counts. I understand the overall structure, and I''ve identified all the necessary steps, so now it is time to write code!


  The embedding path is Anscombe-normalized, and the graph path is log1p-normalized. HVG selection happens independently in each. The graph path is the most interesting path. It applies FWPCA but disabled, which means `alpha_g=0.0`, is going to be applied on the graph path. Next is gene-wise standardization using `sc.pp.scale` with a `max_value` of 10. The graph path is where the PBVE-lite and DAQB come in, with parameters: `temper=0.5` and clamp `[0.8, 1.25]`. The embedding path will utilize `sc.pp.combat`.


  I''ve already got a good foundation with functions I developed during the ALC debugging efforts: `normalize_log1p_inplace`, `_fw_weight_by_var`, `_symmetrize_binary_with_distances`, `build_density_adaptive_bbsg`, and `one_hot_batches`. I can directly use `sc.pp.pca` this time, and I will be using those utility functions with the parameters provided from the archives.


  The main obstacle I''ve identified is the implementation of `_pbve_lite_transform`. It''s not in the usual places. It seems PBVE-lite equalizes the variance of each PC within each batch. So it is just a matter of re-implementing the details: calculate per-batch per-PC variance, global variance, scaling, and tempering. I''ll need to figure out where to get this specific implementation. I''ll search Syntellect''s storage for the function, starting with the location of the core functions. I will scan through the Syntellect storage for those key functions.


  In summary, the key components I need to obtain for implementation are `normalize_total_anscombe_inplace` and `_pbve_lite_transform`. I''ll also ensure to apply all the parameters and use all the functions appropriately. I''ll carefully check HVG selection parameters, as they can sometimes change and impact final performance.

  '
