parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1249\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Lumen I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on shedding light on complex research problems through persistent inquiry and strategic publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 332,880 / 600,000 used (55%)\n- Agent Age: 208 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 16 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive\
    \ communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/syntellect/pbve_lite_module.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/syntellect/pbve_lite_module.py will be displayed\
    \ below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1751 | 1 | PBVE-lite baseline (log1p→PCA80) + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) | Praxis V | 1245 | 0.4739 | 0.478 | 0.689 | 0.205 | 0.244 | 0.947 | 0.669 | 0.000 | 0.981 | 0.023 | 0.504 |\n| 1750 | 1 | PBVE-lite baseline (log1p→PCA60, no HVGs) + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) | Praxis V | 1245 | 0.4636 | 0.425 | 0.567 | 0.200 | 0.263 | 0.940 | 0.648 | 0.000 | 0.973 | 0.005 | 0.615 |\n| 1749 | 1 | DualNorm Generality Test: Anscombe-FWPCA-Combat-Emb & Log1p-FWPCA-BRBG-DAQB-Graph\
    \ | Syntellect II | 1240 | 0.7405 | 0.765 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.965 | 0.723 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.767 |\n| 1748 | 1 | Daedalus V - Final Attempt: Decoupled DualNorm (Anscombe Emb + Simple Graph) | Daedalus V | 1239 | 0.6463 | 0.656 | 0.656 | 0.279 | 0.319 | 0.974 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.983 | 0.109 | 0.758 |\n| 1747 | 1 | DualNorm Generality Baseline: Monolithic Log1p + FWPCA-Combat-Emb & BRBG-DAQB-Graph | Syntellect II | 1239 | 0.7409 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.723 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 1746 | 1 | Daedalus V - Run 13: DualNorm Synthesis (Bugfix Re-run) | Daedalus V | 1237 | 0.6276 | 0.597 | 0.656 | 0.279 | 0.319 | 0.950 | 0.707 | 1.000 | 0.994 | 0.017 | 0.757 |\n| 1745 | 1 | Daedalus V - Run 12: DualNorm Synthesis Attempt | Daedalus V | 1236 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1744 | 1 | ALC SOTA Replication (HVG batch_key=None, alpha_g=0.5, sklearn.Ridge) | Lumen I | 1233 | 0.6921 | 0.774 | 0.181 | 0.271 | 0.400 | 0.967 | 0.731 | 0.783\
    \ | 0.974 | 0.961 | 0.880 |\n| 1743 | 1 | PBVE-lite baseline (log1p→PCA60) + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, euclidean) | Praxis V | 1232 | 0.4679 | 0.458 | 0.652 | 0.210 | 0.235 | 0.935 | 0.666 | 0.000 | 0.973 | 0.024 | 0.525 |\n| 1742 | 1 | PBVE-lite baseline (log1p→PCA60) + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) | Praxis V | 1232 | 0.4661 | 0.452 | 0.652 | 0.210 | 0.235 | 0.945 | 0.659 | 0.000 | 0.979 | 0.021 | 0.509 |\n\nPage 1 of 176 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-176, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/syntellect/pbve_lite_module.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom typing import Literal, Optional\n\ndef _pbve_lite_transform(\n    X: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    temper: float = 0.5,\n    r_min: float = 0.8,\n    r_max: float = 1.25,\n    rng_seed: int = 0,\n    inplace: bool = False,\n) -> np.ndarray:\n\
    \    \"\"\"\n    Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite).\n    Standardizes the variance of each PC across batches.\n\n    Args:\n        X: PCA-reduced data (n_cells x n_components).\n        batches: Array of batch labels for each cell.\n        temper: Tempering factor for variance equalization (0.0 to 1.0).\n        r_min: Minimum scaling factor for PC variance.\n        r_max: Maximum scaling factor for PC variance.\n        rng_seed: Random seed (not used).\n        inplace: If True, modifies X in place. Otherwise, returns a copy.\n\n    Returns:\n        Transformed PCA-reduced data.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not inplace:\n        X = X.copy()\n\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    \n    # Calculate global mean variance across all PCs for reference\n    global_var_mean = np.mean(np.var(X, axis=0))\n    if global_var_mean < 1e-8:\n        global_var_mean = 1.0 # Default if global mean var is ~0\n\n    for batch_id in unique_batches:\n        batch_mask = (batches\
    \ == batch_id)\n        X_batch = X[batch_mask]\n\n        if X_batch.shape[0] > 1: # Need at least 2 samples to compute variance\n            var_per_pc_batch = np.var(X_batch, axis=0)\n            var_per_pc_batch[var_per_pc_batch < 1e-8] = 1e-8 # Clamp min variance\n\n            # s_i = (global_mean_var / batch_var_i)^temper\n            scaling_factors = np.clip(np.power(global_var_mean / var_per_pc_batch, temper), r_min, r_max)\n            \n            # Apply scaling to the batch data\n            X[batch_mask] = X_batch * scaling_factors\n\n    return X\n\ndef _simple_pb_pc_variance_standardization(\n    X: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    target_var: Optional[float] = None, # Target variance for each PC within each batch\n    inplace: bool = False,\n) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Simple Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS).\n    Normalizes the variance of each PC within each batch to a target value.\n    This acts as a preparatory step for PBVE-lite.\n\
    \n    Args:\n        X: PCA-reduced data (n_cells x n_components).\n        batches: Array of batch labels for each cell.\n        target_var: The target variance for each PC within each batch.\n                    If None, uses the mean of overall PC variances.\n        inplace: If True, modifies X in place. Otherwise, returns a copy.\n\n    Returns:\n        Transformed PCA-reduced data with standardized per-batch per-PC variance.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not inplace:\n        X = X.copy()\n\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    \n    # If target_var is None, calculate the mean of overall PC variances from the input data\n    if target_var is None:\n        overall_pc_variances = np.var(X, axis=0)\n        target_var = np.mean(overall_pc_variances)\n        if target_var < 1e-8:\n            target_var = 1.0 # Fallback if data has almost no variance\n\n    for batch_id in unique_batches:\n        batch_mask = (batches == batch_id)\n        X_batch = X[batch_mask]\n\n        if X_batch.shape[0]\
    \ > 1: # Need at least 2 samples to compute variance\n            var_per_pc_batch = np.var(X_batch, axis=0)\n            var_per_pc_batch[var_per_pc_batch < 1e-8] = 1e-8 # Clamp min variance\n\n            # Calculate scaling factor for each PC\n            # s_i = sqrt(target_var / batch_var_i)\n            scaling_factors = np.sqrt(target_var / var_per_pc_batch)\n            \n            # Apply scaling to the batch data\n            X[batch_mask] = X_batch * scaling_factors\n\n    return X\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line\
    \ when executing actions."
