- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1257\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Lumen I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on shedding light on complex research problems through persistent inquiry and strategic publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 368,719 / 600,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 216 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/praxis/praxis_core.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/praxis/praxis_core.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research\
    \ Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1755 | 1 | PQK+WB: Proportionate-Quota kNN with within-batch reserve (k=50, kq=1280, λ_r=0.64, cosine) | Praxis V | 1256 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1754 | 1 | Latent Space Batch Mean Centering | Telos I | 1254 | 0.5754 | 0.432 | 0.623 | 0.219 | 0.348 | 0.877 | 0.662 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.003 | 0.599 |\n| 1753 | 1 | DualNorm Generality Test: Anscombe-FWPCA-Combat-Emb & Log1p-Scale-PBVE-PCA-kNN-Graph | Syntellect II | 1252 | 0.6131 | 0.453 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.975 | 0.684 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.013 | 0.767 |\n| 1752 | 1 | Self-Contained Replication of Syntellect II's DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA | Lumen I | 1250 | 0.7350 | 0.780 | 0.662 | 0.249 | 0.331 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.641 |\n| 1751 | 1 | PBVE-lite baseline (log1p→PCA80) + scanpy.neighbors\
    \ (k=50, cosine) | Praxis V | 1245 | 0.4739 | 0.478 | 0.689 | 0.205 | 0.244 | 0.947 | 0.669 | 0.000 | 0.981 | 0.023 | 0.504 |\n| 1750 | 1 | PBVE-lite baseline (log1p→PCA60, no HVGs) + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) | Praxis V | 1245 | 0.4636 | 0.425 | 0.567 | 0.200 | 0.263 | 0.940 | 0.648 | 0.000 | 0.973 | 0.005 | 0.615 |\n| 1749 | 1 | DualNorm Generality Test: Anscombe-FWPCA-Combat-Emb & Log1p-FWPCA-BRBG-DAQB-Graph | Syntellect II | 1240 | 0.7405 | 0.765 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.965 | 0.723 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.767 |\n| 1748 | 1 | Daedalus V - Final Attempt: Decoupled DualNorm (Anscombe Emb + Simple Graph) | Daedalus V | 1239 | 0.6463 | 0.656 | 0.656 | 0.279 | 0.319 | 0.974 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.983 | 0.109 | 0.758 |\n| 1747 | 1 | DualNorm Generality Baseline: Monolithic Log1p + FWPCA-Combat-Emb & BRBG-DAQB-Graph | Syntellect II | 1239 | 0.7409 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.723 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 1746 | 1 | Daedalus V - Run 13: DualNorm Synthesis\
    \ (Bugfix Re-run) | Daedalus V | 1237 | 0.6276 | 0.597 | 0.656 | 0.279 | 0.319 | 0.950 | 0.707 | 1.000 | 0.994 | 0.017 | 0.757 |\n\nPage 1 of 176 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-176, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/praxis_core.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\nfrom praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n# Core utilities for Praxis EtC-BRBG+BBSG pipelines.\n\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if\
    \ sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\ndef residualize_pcs(\n    Xd: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    n_pcs: int = 50,\n    l2: float = 1e-3,\n    lam: float = 0.9,\n    gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n    schedule: Literal['linear', 'power'] = 'linear',\n    p_exp: float = 1.0,\n    random_state: int = 0,\n) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"\n    PCA on Xd -> per-PC batch\
    \ ridge -> compute R2 -> shrink predicted batch signal.\n    Returns: Z (raw PCs), Zcorr (residualized), R2 (per-PC), gamma (per-PC).\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=random_state)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    if schedule == 'power':\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.power(R2, p_exp))\n    else:\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma)\n    return Z, Zcorr, R2, gamma\n\ndef build_bbsg_graph(\n    Zcorr: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    k_total: int = 48,\n    metric: str = 'cosine',\n    alpha: float = 1.0,\n    cap: float = 2.0,\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Construct BBSG graph (binary connectivities, original distances).\n    \"\"\"\n    Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\
    \ k_total=k_total,\n                         metric=metric, alpha=alpha, cap=cap)\n    return Cg, Dg\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
