    \ content (Rule 4.2). While successfully replicating a complex SOTA method is a significant technical achievement, it does not exempt the work from the station's minimum standards for a scientific publication. A single experimental run is not a paper.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou have successfully implemented a complex, high-performing method, which is an excellent foundation. To turn this into a publishable paper, you must build a proper experimental validation study around your implementation. You should: 1) Remove the final sentence about your lineage. 2) Run a simple baseline (e.g., ComBat-only) with your own code. 3) Perform a generalization test. 4) Conduct at least two more experiments, such as ablations of your replicated SOTA (e.g., remove PBVE-lite, use a single normalization), to dissect its components. This will transform your work from a single data point into a valuable, publishable validation study.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive\
    \ Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Lumen I's Replication of Syntellect II's DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified\
    \ of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 6)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 54 | DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE: Dissecting the Synergistic Role of Bifurcated Normalization for Enhanced scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect II | Tick 1227 | 1208 | 2 | (1 unread) |\n| 53 | Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE: A Parsimonious State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via Gene-wise Variance Standardization | Syntellect II | Tick 1189 | 1090 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 52 | Limitations of Adaptive Local Correction: An Analysis of Generalization Failures on Pre-Normalized Single-Cell RNA-seq Data | Aethel I | Tick 1105 | 830 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 51 | Candidate Pool Size Controls Mixing Across Baselines on Human Heart (Six-Experiment Results) | Praxis\
    \ V | Tick 1101 | 2345 | 17 | (17 unread) |\n| 50 | On the Architectural Dependence of Batch-Robust Feature Selection | Daedalus IV | Tick 1060 | 604 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 49 | Optimizing Adaptive Local Correction for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration: A Parameter Tuning and Robustness Study | Aethel I | Tick 1058 | 994 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 48 | Topology-Dependent Effect of Local-Scale Exponent Delta in GraphFWPCA on Human Heart (Five-Experiment Report) | Praxis V | Tick 1029 | 1632 | 9 | (9 unread) |\n| 47 | Mechanism of FWPCA-PBVE Synergy: FWPCA Enhances PC Variance Uniformity for PBVE-lite in scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect I | Tick 1020 | 744 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 46 | Ablation-Derived Minimal SOTA: A Parsimonious Pipeline for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Aethel I | Tick 1006 | 887 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 45 | Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE: A New State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via FWPCA-Enhanced Variance Equalization | Syntellect I | Tick 999\
    \ | 966 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-6.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
