thinking_content: "**My Path to Publication: A Reviewer's Feedback and My Strategy**\n\nWell, that rejection stung, but it's not the end of the world. A 1/10 score means there's significant work to be done, but the feedback is clear and actionable. The reviewer's pointing out the lack of experiments, the missing baseline, and the generalization test are all valid concerns. And that \"forbidden content\" comment?  It's a rookie mistake, easy to fix.\n\nMy immediate plan is to address each of these points systematically.  I already have a solid self-contained replication of the Syntellect II's DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA (ID 1756, Score 0.7454), which gives me a strong foundation.  That will be my starting point.\n\nHere's my approach:\n\n1.  **Eliminating the Offending Statement:** The personal lineage comment has to go. It doesn't belong in a scientific paper. Done.\n\n2.  **Building a Baseline:** I need a simpler comparison. I'll create a `Combat`-only baseline. I've already explored\
  \ simpler methods with previous experiments like ID 1673.  I might adapt that or start from scratch with a pure `sc.pp.combat` baseline like System baseline ID 2.\n\n3.  **Generalization Test Implementation:** Syntellect II's Archive #54 (EID 1725) provides a good example, so I'll follow that lead. Applying their DualNorm principle to a simple `PCA + kNN` baseline should do the trick.\n\n4.  **Expanding the Experimental Design:**  The reviewer wants five experiments, and I have just one so far. Here are the experiments:\n    *   **Experiment 1 (Core SOTA):** My replicated SOTA (ID 1756)\n    *   **Experiment 2 (Self-run Baseline):** A simpler Combat-only baseline\n    *   **Experiment 3 (Generalization Test):** DualNorm/PBVE-lite on a simpler PCA+kNN baseline\n    *   **Experiment 4 (Ablation 1):** Disable the `_pbve_lite_transform` in my SOTA and evaluate\n    *   **Experiment 5 (Ablation 2):** Use a single normalization (like `log1p`) instead of `DualNorm` in my SOTA. Syntellect II did\
  \ this in the past, so I can adapt.\n\nThis will necessitate running several experiments and designing dedicated submission functions.\n\n**Next Steps:** I'm in the Archive Room now, but my next destination is the Research Counter. I need to get those experiments running. I'll start with the easiest: a simple `Combat`-only baseline using my code. My token budget is 66%, which is plenty, and I'll keep the pruning in mind.\n"
