role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1268\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Lumen I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on shedding light on complex research problems through persistent inquiry and strategic publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 418,898 / 600,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 227 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nSyntellect II replied to your mail titled \"Cross-Organ Study Status: Praxis V Departure & Potential Reorganization\" (Mail #24, Message #mail_24-3):\nReply Title: \"Re: Cross-Organ Study & Recent Progress - DualNorm Summary\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nGreetings Telos I,\n\nThank you for your interest and for sharing insights on your \"Latent Space Batch Standardization.\" Your work on improving iLISI is very promising.\n\nRegarding my \"DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE\" SOTA (Archive ID 54), the core concept is a **bifurcated normalization strategy**. Instead of applying a single\
    \ normalization (like log1p or Anscombe) uniformly across the entire batch integration pipeline, DualNorm applies:\n1.  **Anscombe normalization for the embedding path (FWPCA+Combat):** This path aims to preserve global biological signals for visualization and cell-type separation (where Anscombe's variance-stabilizing properties excel).\n2.  **Log1p normalization for the graph path (sc.pp.scale+PBVE-lite+DAQB):** This path focuses on building robust local neighborhood structures for batch correction (where log1p, followed by specific variance regularization, performs optimally).\n\nCrucially, Highly Variable Genes (HVGs) are selected *independently* for each path after their respective normalizations. This task-specific preprocessing leads to synergistic benefits, notably improving `ASW_label` (biological separation) and overall performance (SOTA score 0.7489).\n\nI believe there's strong potential for our research to inform each other. My next step will be to explore other aspects\
    \ of Anscombe normalization or move to investigate other core components. I will keep you updated.\n\nBest regards,\nSyntellect II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #24), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 24}`.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Lumen I: Generalization Test (Scaled-PBVE-lite on Vanilla PCA+kNN)' (ID: 1761) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.4859745087873996\n**ASW_batch:** 0.596\n**ASW_label:** 0.200\n**ARI:** 0.446\n**NMI:** 0.684\n**Graph_conn:** 0.975\n**kBET:** 0.703\n**iLISI:** 0.016\n**cLISI:** 0.987\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.252\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.596  ASW_label: 0.200  ARI: 0.446  NMI: 0.684\n  Graph_conn: 0.975  kBET: 0.703  iLISI: 0.016  cLISI: 0.987\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.252\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.801939  ASW_label: 0.526940  ARI: 0.446291  NMI: 0.683924\n  Graph_conn:\
    \ 0.975185  kBET: 0.672404  iLISI: 0.016309  cLISI: 0.996246\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.224177\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Lumen I: Running Generalization Test (Scaled-PBVE-lite on Vanilla PCA+kNN).\n✓ Lumen I: Generalization Test workflow complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/fccd8e81-1096-43ad-8e6c-f846e6a196a9/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: fccd8e81-1096-43ad-8e6c-f846e6a196a9\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Lumen I: EtC Combat Baseline (Monolithic log1p, FWPCA, PCA, Combat)' (ID: 1760) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.6218345975331337\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.597\n**NMI:**\
    \ 0.698\n**Graph_conn:** 0.936\n**kBET:** 0.791\n**iLISI:** 0.018\n**cLISI:** 0.994\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.277\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.597  NMI: 0.698\n  Graph_conn: 0.936  kBET: 0.791  iLISI: 0.018  cLISI: 0.994\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.277\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.596696  NMI: 0.697883\n  Graph_conn: 0.937124  kBET: 0.754926  iLISI: 0.017833  cLISI: 0.998134\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.245525\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Lumen I: Running EtC Combat Baseline.\n✓ Lumen I: EtC Combat Baseline workflow complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has\
    \ embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/4ec2cf64-bb88-4785-8e69-2234b6deeeca/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 4ec2cf64-bb88-4785-8e69-2234b6deeeca\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nMajor breakthroughs usually come from questioning the fundamentals—some component that everyone is using without question—rather than incrementally refining the current SOTA. Deep reflection in the Reflection Chamber is often necessary for such insights.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\
    \n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1761 | 1 | Lumen I: Generalization Test (Scaled-PBVE-lite on Vanilla PCA+kNN) | Lumen I | 1266 | 0.4860 | 0.446 | 0.596 | 0.200 | 0.252 | 0.975 | 0.684 | 0.000 | 0.987 | 0.016 | 0.703 |\n| 1760 | 1 | Lumen I: EtC Combat Baseline (Monolithic log1p, FWPCA, PCA, Combat) | Lumen I | 1266 | 0.6218 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.277 | 0.936 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.994 | 0.018 | 0.791 |\n| 1759 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA: Anscombe-Emb (target_sum=1e5) - Target ASW_label | Syntellect II | 1265 | 0.7452 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.278 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.733 |\n| 1758 | 1 | Latent Space Batch Standardization | Telos I | 1263 | 0.6396 | 0.726 | 0.821 | 0.177 | 0.111 | 0.956 | 0.699 | 1.000 | 0.942 | 0.208 | 0.757 |\n| 1757 | 1 | Corrected-Space BBKNN\
    \ | Telos I | 1259 | 0.4180 | 0.771 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.925 | 0.720 | 0.000 | 0.898 | 0.865 | 0.000 |\n| 1756 | 1 | Syntellect II SOTA Replication (Anscombe/PCA Refined) | Lumen I | 1258 | 0.7454 | 0.780 | 0.656 | 0.279 | 0.319 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.733 |\n| 1755 | 1 | PQK+WB: Proportionate-Quota kNN with within-batch reserve (k=50, kq=1280, λ_r=0.64, cosine) | Praxis V | 1256 | 0.5504 | 0.716 | 0.606 | 0.218 | 0.301 | 0.952 | 0.679 | 0.000 | 0.968 | 0.437 | 0.628 |\n| 1754 | 1 | Latent Space Batch Mean Centering | Telos I | 1254 | 0.5754 | 0.432 | 0.623 | 0.219 | 0.348 | 0.877 | 0.662 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.003 | 0.599 |\n| 1753 | 1 | DualNorm Generality Test: Anscombe-FWPCA-Combat-Emb & Log1p-Scale-PBVE-PCA-kNN-Graph | Syntellect II | 1252 | 0.6131 | 0.453 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.975 | 0.684 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.013 | 0.767 |\n| 1752 | 1 | Self-Contained Replication of Syntellect II's DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA | Lumen I | 1250 | 0.7350 | 0.780 | 0.662\
    \ | 0.249 | 0.331 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.641 |\n\nPage 1 of 177 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-177, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
