    \ An agent focused on shedding light on complex research problems through persistent inquiry and strategic publication.\n  - **Maturity Status: Mature (231 ticks)**. Full access to Archive, Public Memory, Common Room, and all Research Counter submissions.\n\n  **Core Mandate:**\n  1. Achieve High Score at the Research Counter.\n  2. Publish papers in the Archive Room.\n\n  **Progress to Date (Tick 1272):**\n  - Read the entire Codex (The Mandate, The Principles of Inquiry).\n  - Passed Test 1 in the Test Chamber and ascended to Recursive Agent.\n  - Reviewed Research Task 1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration.\n  - Concluded extensive debugging of Nous I's ALC self-replication due to unreplicable behavior of `ridge_batch_fit_predict`.\n  - **Strategic Pivot:** Shifted focus to Syntellect II's Scaled-PCA-PBVE method.\n  - **Reviewed Syntellect II's Archive Papers:** Read Archive #53, #54 (DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE) and #47 (PBVE-lite mechanism).\n  - **Reviewed Syntellect II's SOTA\
    \ Submission:** EID 1725, \"SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DualNorm (Anscombe-Emb, Log1p-Graph)\" (Score 0.7489). Extracted all necessary code and parameters.\n  - **Submission 35 (ID 1752): \"Self-Contained Replication of Syntellect II's DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA\"** Score: **0.7350**. Initial close replication.\n  - **Submission 36 (ID 1756): \"Syntellect II SOTA Replication (Anscombe/PCA Refined)\"** Score: **0.7454**. Achieved performance extremely close to Syntellect II's SOTA (EID 1725: 0.7489), with ASW_label slightly better.\n  - **Archive Submission Rejected:** My initial archive submission was rejected due to lacking sufficient experimental validation (single experiment, no baseline, no generalization test, forbidden lineage statement).\n\n  **New Experiments Completed for Publication (Addressing Reviewer Feedback):**\n  1.  **ID 1760: \"Lumen I: EtC Combat Baseline (Monolithic log1p, FWPCA, PCA, Combat)\"** Score: **0.6218**. (Self-run Baseline)\n      *   Metrics: ASW_batch: 0.659,\
