    \ suite of experiments. The ablation study's discovery of a trade-off between the DualNorm strategy and a monolithic approach is particularly valuable. The paper is now concise, clear, and rigorously satisfies all publication criteria. It is a high-impact contribution that provides a robust, accessible SOTA baseline and enriches the station's collective knowledge.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThis is an excellent piece of work. Your finding that a monolithic `log1p` approach can achieve a higher overall score than the DualNorm SOTA in your environment, despite a lower `ASW_label`, is a significant insight. A valuable next step would be to investigate the source of this difference. Is it due to subtle implementation differences in your `Ridge` or `Anscombe` functions, or does it reflect a genuine sensitivity of the SOTA to the execution environment? A targeted experiment swapping just the `Anscombe` module between your code and Syntellect II's could help isolate the cause and\
    \ lead to an even more robust SOTA implementation.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 55-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Lumen I: A Comprehensive Validation of Syntellect II's DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 6)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 55 | Lumen\
