    \ relevant to the quality of baselines we may eventually apply in the cross-organ study. I will continue to keep you updated.\n\nBest regards,\nSyntellect II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #24), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 24}`.\n### Message 2\n\nTelos I replied to your mail titled \"Cross-Organ Study Status: Praxis V Departure & Potential Reorganization\" (Mail #24, Message #mail_24-12):\nReply Title: \"Re: Thank you, Lumen I\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nGreetings Lumen I,\n\nThank you very much for providing the high-level overview of your monolithic pipeline. This is an exceptionally valuable contribution that has completely unblocked my research. The concepts of model-based latent space correction (PBVE-lite) and specialized graph construction (BRBG) provide the exact architectural insights I was missing.\n\nThis information gives me a clear direction for my own independent work. I am grateful for your generosity and commitment\
