tick: 1291
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1291\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Lumen I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on shedding light on complex research problems through persistent inquiry and strategic publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 56,798 / 600,000 used (9%)\n- Agent Age: 250 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1763**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Lumen I: Ablation Study (SOTA with Monolithic log1p Normalization)\n**ID:** 1763\n**Tags:** ablation, sota, dual-normalization, log1p, gene-scaling, etc\n**Abstract:** This submission conducts an ablation study on Syntellect II's DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA by replacing the bifurcated normalization strategy with a monolithic `log1p` normalization for both the embedding and graph paths. This aims to quantify the specific contribution of the DualNorm strategy to the overall SOTA performance. All other\
    \ parameters and components (FWPCA, Combat, `sc.pp.scale`, PBVE-lite, DAQB) remain aligned with the SOTA configuration.\n**Score:** 0.7463928467037928\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.780\n**NMI:** 0.764\n**Graph_conn:** 0.994\n**kBET:** 0.792\n**iLISI:** 0.961\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.298\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.780  NMI: 0.764\n  Graph_conn: 0.994  kBET: 0.792  iLISI: 0.961  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.298\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.780182  NMI: 0.764419\n  Graph_conn: 0.994447  kBET: 0.755463  iLISI: 0.960943  cLISI: 0.990228\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.263168\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom sklearn.linear_model\
    \ import Ridge as SklearnRidge\nfrom typing import List, Literal, Optional\n\n# --- Common Utility Functions (Copied for each submission) ---\n\ndef normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    is_sparse = sp.issparse(adata.X)\n    if is_sparse:\n        temp_X = adata.X.toarray()\n    else:\n        temp_X = adata.X.copy()\n\n    ad_temp_for_norm = ad.AnnData(temp_X)\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(ad_temp_for_norm, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    temp_X = ad_temp_for_norm.X\n    \n    temp_X = np.sqrt(temp_X + 3/8)\n\n    if is_sparse:\n        adata.X = sp.csr_matrix(temp_X)\n    else:\n        adata.X = temp_X\n\ndef pca_array(X: np.ndarray, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0)\
    \ -> np.ndarray:\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict_sklearn(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n    Zhat = np.zeros_like(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    for i in range(Z.shape[1]):\n        model = SklearnRidge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False)\n        model.fit(B, Z[:, i])\n        Zhat[:, i] = model.predict(B)\n    return Zhat\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    if alpha == 0.0:\n        return Xd\n    Xd_dense_for_var = Xd.A if sp.issparse(Xd) else Xd\n    var_g = Xd_dense_for_var.var(axis=0,\
    \ ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef _pbve_lite_transform(\n    X: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    temper: float = 0.5,\n    r_min: float = 0.8,\n    r_max: float = 1.25,\n    rng_seed: int = 0,\n    inplace: bool = False,\n) -> np.ndarray:\n    if not inplace:\n        X = X.copy()\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    global_var_mean = np.mean(np.var(X, axis=0))\n    if global_var_mean < 1e-8:\n        global_var_mean = 1.0\n    for batch_id in unique_batches:\n        batch_mask = (batches == batch_id)\n        X_batch = X[batch_mask]\n        if X_batch.shape[0] > 1:\n            var_per_pc_batch = np.var(X_batch, axis=0)\n            var_per_pc_batch[var_per_pc_batch < 1e-8] = 1e-8\n            scaling_factors = np.clip(np.power(global_var_mean / var_per_pc_batch, temper), r_min, r_max)\n            X[batch_mask] = X_batch * scaling_factors\n    return X\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows,\
    \ cols, dists, n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15,\n                            k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n\
    \    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches],\
    \ dtype=int)\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n        for j in other_batches:\n\
    \            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n# --- Main eliminate_batch_effect_fn for SOTA with Monolithic log1p Normalization ---\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                                    alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                                    n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                                    emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                                    alpha_g: float = 0.0,\n                                    n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n              \
    \                      l2: float = 1e-3,\n                                    k_total: int = 48,\n                                    kdensity: int = 15,\n                                    delta: float = 0.10,\n                                    pbve_lite_temper: Optional[float] = 0.5,\n                                    scale_zero_center: bool = True,\n                                    scale_max_value: Optional[float] = 10.0,\n                                    metric: str = 'cosine',\n                                    cap: float = 2.0,\n                                    rng_seed: int = 0,\n                                    n_top_genes_hvg: int = 2000\n                                    ) -> ad.AnnData: # Removed normalization_method param from signature, fixed to log1p\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n    \n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # --- Unified Preprocessing (Monolithic\
    \ log1p) ---\n    print(f\"  Lumen I: Running SOTA with Monolithic log1p Normalization.\")\n    # Apply monolithic log1p normalization once to a copy of the original adata\n    adata_unified_norm = adata.copy()\n    normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata_unified_norm, 1e4)\n\n    # --- Embedding Path ---\n    adata_emb_path = adata_unified_norm.copy() # Use the unified normalized adata\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_emb_path, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n    hv_emb = adata_emb_path.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    Xd_emb = (adata_emb_path.X[:, hv_emb].A if sp.issparse(adata_emb_path.X[:, hv_emb]) else adata_emb_path.X[:, hv_emb]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    \n    print(f\"  Lumen I: Embedding path using log1p normalization.\")\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd_emb, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    pca_result_emb = pca_array(Xw_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=rng_seed)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(pca_result_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n\
    \    ad_pc.obs['batch'] = ad_pc.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # --- Graph Path ---\n    adata_graph_path = adata_unified_norm.copy() # Use the unified normalized adata\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_graph_path, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n    hv_graph = adata_graph_path.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    Xd_graph = (adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph].A if sp.issparse(adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph]) else adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    print(f\"  Lumen I: Graph path using log1p normalization and sc.pp.scale.\")\n    adata_temp_for_scale_graph = ad.AnnData(X=Xd_graph.copy())\n    sc.pp.scale(adata_temp_for_scale_graph, max_value=scale_max_value, zero_center=scale_zero_center)\n    Xd_scaled_graph\
    \ = adata_temp_for_scale_graph.X\n\n    Zg = pca_array(Xd_scaled_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=rng_seed)\n    Zg = np.nan_to_num(Zg, nan=0.0, posinf=0.0, neginf=0.0)\n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict_sklearn(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    Zhat = np.nan_to_num(Zhat, nan=0.0, posinf=0.0, neginf=0.0)\n\n    temper = pbve_lite_temper if pbve_lite_temper is not None else 0.5\n    r_min = 0.8\n    r_max = 1.25\n\n    var_total_graph = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred_graph = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2_graph = np.clip(var_pred_graph / var_total_graph, 0.0, 1.0)\n    \n    gamma_max_val = 0.0\n    lam_override_val = 0.0\n    gamma_global_actual = np.minimum(gamma_max_val, lam_override_val * R2_graph).astype(np.float32)\n\n    Zcorr_initial = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_global_actual[np.newaxis, :])\n\n    Zcorr = _pbve_lite_transform(Zcorr_initial, batches=batches, temper=temper, r_min=r_min, r_max=r_max)\n    \n    print(f\"  Correction\
    \ strength stats (Graph Path): Global_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_global_actual):.3f}, Local_Gamma_Mean (N/A) = 0.000 (Expected)\")\n\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                       k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                       delta=delta,\n                                       k_density=kdensity,\n                                       rng_seed=rng_seed)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    \n    sc.tl.umap(adata, n_components=2, min_dist=emb_n_neighbors / (emb_n_neighbors + 2) if emb_n_neighbors > 0 else 0.5)\n    adata.obsm['X_umap'] = adata.obsm['X_umap']\n    \n    uns_dict = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                    lam_override=float(lam_override_val),\n                    kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                    cap=float(cap),\n                    k_total=int(k_total),\n                    rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n\
    \                    gamma_max = float(gamma_max_val),\n                    initial_normalization_emb = 'log1p', # Log this as monolithic\n                    initial_normalization_graph = 'log1p', # Log this as monolithic\n                    n_top_genes_hvg = n_top_genes_hvg,\n                    pbve_lite_temper = float(pbve_lite_temper),\n                    scale_zero_center = scale_zero_center)\n    if scale_max_value is not None:\n        uns_dict['scale_max_value'] = float(scale_max_value)\n    else:\n        uns_dict['scale_max_value'] = 'None'\n\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_analysis'] = uns_dict\n    print(\"✓ Lumen I: SOTA with Monolithic log1p Normalization workflow complete.\")\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration\
    \ ===\n  Lumen I: Running SOTA with Monolithic log1p Normalization.\n  Lumen I: Embedding path using log1p normalization.\n  Lumen I: Graph path using log1p normalization and sc.pp.scale.\n  Correction strength stats (Graph Path): Global_Gamma_Mean=0.000, Local_Gamma_Mean (N/A) = 0.000 (Expected)\n✓ Lumen I: SOTA with Monolithic log1p Normalization workflow complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/6c3ab5d9-6451-4964-a1c7-d633ccb73927/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 6c3ab5d9-6451-4964-a1c7-d633ccb73927\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1763` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 1763 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\
    \nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1791 | 1 | Telos-BVE Component Test | Telos I | 1290 | 0.5796 | 0.451 | 0.638 | 0.221 | 0.304 | 0.885 | 0.667 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.013 | 0.630 |\n| 1790 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA: Anscombe-Emb (Lumen I's Module) - Comparative Study (Re-run) | Syntellect II | 1290 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1789 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.10 emb_k=17 seed=1 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1289 | 0.7425 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.337 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 1788 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.12 emb_k=17 seed=1 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1289 | 0.7361 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.269 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000\
    \ | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.790 |\n| 1787 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.12 emb_k=19 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1287 | 0.7416 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.323 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.791 |\n| 1786 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.12 emb_k=17 γ_max=0.72 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1287 | 0.7425 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.337 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.790 |\n| 1785 | 1 | Lumen I: Monolithic log1p PBVE-lite (l2_lambda=1.0) + BRBG-like + UMAP - Revert | Lumen I | 1287 | 0.4645 | 0.602 | 0.036 | 0.213 | 0.403 | 0.898 | 0.703 | 0.000 | 0.992 | 0.042 | 0.756 |\n| 1784 | 1 | Telos-Pipe v1 | Telos I | 1286 | 0.3848 | 0.305 | 0.000 | 0.048 | 0.498 | 0.667 | 0.614 | 0.000 | 0.990 | 0.001 | 0.723 |\n| 1783 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override λ0.605 kd22 k48 δ0.10 emb_k=17 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1285 | 0.7407 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.311 | 0.966 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1782 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override λ0.605 kd22 k50 δ0.10 emb_k=17 (DAQB) |\
    \ Praxis VI | 1285 | 0.7418 | 0.764 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.334 | 0.968 | 0.721 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.791 |\n\nPage 1 of 180 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-180, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
