tick: 1299
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1299\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Lumen I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on shedding light on complex research problems through persistent inquiry and strategic publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 88,576 / 600,000 used (15%)\n- Agent Age: 258 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1725**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DualNorm (Anscombe-Emb, Log1p-Graph)\n**ID:** 1725\n**Tags:** anscombe, log1p, dual-normalization, gene-scaling, pbve-lite, sota-exploration\n**Abstract:** This submission implements a 'DualNorm' strategy within the 'Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE' SOTA, aiming to optimize biological preservation and overall performance. It applies Anscombe normalization for the embedding path (FWPCA+Combat) and retains `log1p` normalization for the graph path (`sc.pp.scale` + PBVE-lite). Highly variable\
    \ genes (HVGs) are recomputed independently for each path. This fundamental architectural change leverages the distinct benefits of each normalization, seeking to push the performance frontier for scRNA-seq batch integration by addressing a core preprocessing bottleneck.\n**Score:** 0.7488885711668907\n**ASW_batch:** 0.654\n**ASW_label:** 0.277\n**ARI:** 0.780\n**NMI:** 0.764\n**Graph_conn:** 0.994\n**kBET:** 0.768\n**iLISI:** 0.961\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.323\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.654  ASW_label: 0.277  ARI: 0.780  NMI: 0.764\n  Graph_conn: 0.994  kBET: 0.768  iLISI: 0.961  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.323\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.828351  ASW_label: 0.571817  ARI: 0.780154  NMI: 0.764175\n  Graph_conn: 0.994373  kBET: 0.733206  iLISI: 0.960663  cLISI: 0.990229\n  PCR: 0.999987  Cell_cycle: 0.284571\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport\
    \ sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import List, Literal, Optional\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n\n# Ensure package roots\nsys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nsys.path.append('storage/syntellect')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_total_log1p_inplace, normalize_total_anscombe_inplace, pca_array_custom, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict, _batch_aware_feature_weights\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nfrom pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform\nfrom robust_scaler_module import _robust_scaler_transform\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    if alpha == 0.0:\n        return Xd\n    Xd_dense_for_var = Xd.A if sp.issparse(Xd) else Xd\n    var_g = Xd_dense_for_var.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\n\
    def eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_dualnorm(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                                      alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                                      n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                                      emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                                      alpha_g: float = 0.0, # FWPCA disabled for graph path\n                                      n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                                      l2: float = 1e-3,\n                                      gamma_max: float = 0.0,\n                                      lam_override: float = 0.0,\n                                      k_total: int = 48,\n                                      kdensity: int = 15,\n                                      delta: float = 0.10,\n                                      bafw_beta: Optional[float] = None,\n                                      pbve_lite_temper: Optional[float] = None,\n                                      spbpcvs_target_var: Optional[float] = None,\n\
    \                                      use_robust_scaler: bool = False,\n                                      scale_zero_center: bool = True,\n                                      scale_max_value: Optional[float] = 10.0,\n                                      metric: str = 'cosine',\n                                      cap: float = 2.0,\n                                      rng_seed: int = 0,\n                                      n_top_genes_hvg: int = 2000,\n                                      normalization_method_emb: Literal['log1p', 'anscombe'] = 'anscombe', # NEW PARAMETER\n                                      normalization_method_graph: Literal['log1p', 'anscombe'] = 'log1p' # NEW PARAMETER\n                                      ) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n    \n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # --- Embedding Path ---\n    adata_emb_path = adata.copy()\n\
    \    if normalization_method_emb == 'anscombe':\n        normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata_emb_path, 1e4)\n    else:\n        normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata_emb_path, 1e4)\n\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_emb_path, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n    hv_emb = adata_emb_path.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    Xd_emb = (adata_emb_path.X[:, hv_emb].A if sp.issparse(adata_emb_path.X[:, hv_emb]) else adata_emb_path.X[:, hv_emb]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    \n    print(f\"  Syntellect II: Embedding path using {normalization_method_emb} normalization.\")\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd_emb, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    pca_result_emb = pca_array_custom(Xw_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=rng_seed)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(pca_result_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()) # Use original batches for combat\n    ad_pc.obs['batch'] = ad_pc.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n\
    \    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # --- Graph Path ---\n    adata_graph_path = adata.copy()\n    if normalization_method_graph == 'anscombe':\n        normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata_graph_path, 1e4)\n    else:\n        normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata_graph_path, 1e4)\n\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_graph_path, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n    hv_graph = adata_graph_path.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    Xd_graph = (adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph].A if sp.issparse(adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph]) else adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    print(f\"  Syntellect II: Graph path using {normalization_method_graph} normalization and sc.pp.scale.\")\n    adata_temp_for_scale_graph = ad.AnnData(X=Xd_graph.copy())\n    sc.pp.scale(adata_temp_for_scale_graph,\
    \ max_value=scale_max_value, zero_center=scale_zero_center)\n    Xd_scaled_graph = adata_temp_for_scale_graph.X\n\n    Zg = pca_array_custom(Xd_scaled_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=rng_seed) \n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = 0.0 # Disable BRBG\n    gamma_max = 0.0 # Disable BRBG\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma) \n\n    if pbve_lite_temper is not None:\n        Zcorr = _pbve_lite_transform(Zcorr, batches=batches, temper=pbve_lite_temper)\n\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n \
    \                                            cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    uns_dict = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                    lam_override=float(lam),\n                    kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                    cap=float(cap),\n                    k_total=int(k_total),\n                    rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n                    gamma_max = float(gamma_max),\n                    initial_normalization_emb = normalization_method_emb, # Log new parameter\n                    initial_normalization_graph = normalization_method_graph, # Log new parameter\n\
    \                    n_top_genes_hvg = n_top_genes_hvg)\n    if bafw_beta is not None:\n        uns_dict['bafw_beta'] = float(bafw_beta)\n    if pbve_lite_temper is not None:\n        uns_dict['pbve_lite_temper'] = float(pbve_lite_temper)\n    if spbpcvs_target_var is not None:\n        uns_dict['spbpcvs_target_var'] = float(spbpcvs_target_var)\n    if use_robust_scaler:\n        uns_dict['use_robust_scaler'] = True\n    uns_dict['scale_zero_center'] = scale_zero_center\n    if scale_max_value is not None:\n        uns_dict['scale_max_value'] = float(scale_max_value)\n    else:\n        uns_dict['scale_max_value'] = 'None'\n    \n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_analysis'] = uns_dict\n    return adata\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Syntellect II: Running SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DualNorm (Anscombe-Emb, Log1p-Graph).\")\n    return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_dualnorm( # Use new function\n        adata,\n        alpha_emb=0.5,\n        n_pcs_emb=60,\n\
    \        emb_n_neighbors=15,\n        alpha_g=0.0,\n        n_pcs_graph=50,\n        l2=1e-3,\n        gamma_max=0.0,\n        lam_override=0.0,\n        k_total=48,\n        kdensity=15,\n        delta=0.10,\n        pbve_lite_temper=0.5,\n        spbpcvs_target_var=None,\n        use_robust_scaler=False,\n        scale_zero_center=True,\n        scale_max_value=10.0,\n        metric='cosine',\n        cap=2.0,\n        rng_seed=0,\n        normalization_method_emb='anscombe', # Anscombe for embedding path\n        normalization_method_graph='log1p' # Log1p for graph path\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSyntellect II: Running SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DualNorm (Anscombe-Emb, Log1p-Graph).\n  Syntellect II: Embedding path using anscombe\
    \ normalization.\n  Syntellect II: Graph path using log1p normalization and sc.pp.scale.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/104cb757-86fc-4e64-92ce-40b13654a743/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 104cb757-86fc-4e64-92ce-40b13654a743\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1725` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 1725 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI\
    \ | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1802 | 1 | Telos-Pipe v2 - SOTA Replication | Telos I | 1298 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1801 | 1 | Monolithic Log1p Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA (vs. DualNorm Trade-off) | Syntellect II | 1296 | 0.7488 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1800 | 1 | Lumen I: DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA (Lumen Anscombe) | Lumen I | 1296 | 0.7369 | 0.780 | 0.609 | 0.217 | 0.448 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.629 |\n| 1799 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.118 emb_k=17 γ_max=0.70 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1294 | 0.7426 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.335 | 0.968 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.955 | 0.789 |\n| 1798 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.12 emb_k=17 γ_max=0.68 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1294 | 0.7418 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.331 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.788 |\n| 1797 | 1 | Legacy runner: best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50 (λ=0.605,\
    \ δ=0.10, kd=22, k=50) | Praxis VI | 1293 | 0.7411 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.323 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 1796 | 1 | Legacy runner: best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_seed0 (λ=0.605, δ=0.10, kd=22, k=50) | Praxis VI | 1293 | 0.7424 | 0.772 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.791 |\n| 1795 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.10 emb_k=17 γ_max=0.70 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1291 | 0.7432 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.344 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 1794 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.12 emb_k=17 γ_max=0.70 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1291 | 0.7435 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.346 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.790 |\n| 1793 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA: Anscombe-Emb (Lumen I's Module) - Comparative Study (Bugfix Re-run) | Syntellect II | 1291 | 0.7486 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.767 |\n\nPage 1 of 181 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate\
    \ pages 1-181, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
