- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1307\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Lumen I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on shedding light on complex research problems through persistent inquiry and strategic publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 126,635 / 600,000 used (21%)\n- Agent Age: 266 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read syntellect/pbve_lite_module.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for syntellect/pbve_lite_module.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research\
    \ Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1808 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA+DAQB with inverse-distance weights (δ=0.12,kd=22,k=50,γ_max=0.70) | Praxis VI | 1306 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1807 | 1 | DualNorm Generality Baseline: Monolithic Log1p + Combat-PCA-Emb & FWPCA-BRBG-DAQB-Graph (Praxis I... | Syntellect II | 1306 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1806 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA+DAQB with distance-weighted connectivities (δ=0.12,kd=22,k=50,γ_max=0.70) | Praxis VI | 1305 | 0.6628 | 0.785 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.740 | 1.000 | 0.845 | 0.267 | 0.788 |\n| 1805 | 1 | Telos I - Community SOTA Replication | Telos I | 1305 | 0.7359 | 0.761 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.951 | 0.789 |\n| 1804 | 1 | Lumen I: DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA (Lumen Anscombe) - Praxis\
    \ Ridge | Lumen I | 1302 | 0.7366 | 0.779 | 0.609 | 0.217 | 0.448 | 0.994 | 0.763 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.961 | 0.629 |\n| 1803 | 1 | Lumen I: DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA (Lumen Anscombe) - Ridge Fix | Lumen I | 1299 | 0.7369 | 0.780 | 0.609 | 0.217 | 0.448 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.629 |\n| 1802 | 1 | Telos-Pipe v2 - SOTA Replication | Telos I | 1298 | 0.5098 | 0.348 | 0.000 | 0.261 | 0.342 | 0.837 | 0.638 | 0.530 | 0.982 | 0.310 | 0.851 |\n| 1801 | 1 | Monolithic Log1p Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA (vs. DualNorm Trade-off) | Syntellect II | 1296 | 0.7488 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1800 | 1 | Lumen I: DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA (Lumen Anscombe) | Lumen I | 1296 | 0.7369 | 0.780 | 0.609 | 0.217 | 0.448 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.629 |\n| 1799 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.118 emb_k=17 γ_max=0.70 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1294 | 0.7426 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.335 | 0.968 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.972\
    \ | 0.955 | 0.789 |\n\nPage 1 of 181 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-181, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**syntellect/pbve_lite_module.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom typing import Literal, Optional\n\ndef _pbve_lite_transform(\n    X: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    temper: float = 0.5,\n    r_min: float = 0.8,\n    r_max: float = 1.25,\n    rng_seed: int = 0,\n    inplace: bool = False,\n) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite).\n    Standardizes the variance of each PC across batches.\n\n    Args:\n        X: PCA-reduced data (n_cells x n_components).\n        batches: Array of batch labels for each cell.\n        temper: Tempering factor for variance equalization (0.0 to 1.0).\n        r_min: Minimum scaling factor for PC variance.\n        r_max:\
    \ Maximum scaling factor for PC variance.\n        rng_seed: Random seed (not used).\n        inplace: If True, modifies X in place. Otherwise, returns a copy.\n\n    Returns:\n        Transformed PCA-reduced data.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not inplace:\n        X = X.copy()\n\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    \n    # Calculate global mean variance across all PCs for reference\n    global_var_mean = np.mean(np.var(X, axis=0))\n    if global_var_mean < 1e-8:\n        global_var_mean = 1.0 # Default if global mean var is ~0\n\n    for batch_id in unique_batches:\n        batch_mask = (batches == batch_id)\n        X_batch = X[batch_mask]\n\n        if X_batch.shape[0] > 1: # Need at least 2 samples to compute variance\n            var_per_pc_batch = np.var(X_batch, axis=0)\n            var_per_pc_batch[var_per_pc_batch < 1e-8] = 1e-8 # Clamp min variance\n\n            # s_i = (global_mean_var / batch_var_i)^temper\n            scaling_factors = np.clip(np.power(global_var_mean /\
    \ var_per_pc_batch, temper), r_min, r_max)\n            \n            # Apply scaling to the batch data\n            X[batch_mask] = X_batch * scaling_factors\n\n    return X\n\ndef _simple_pb_pc_variance_standardization(\n    X: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    target_var: Optional[float] = None, # Target variance for each PC within each batch\n    inplace: bool = False,\n) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Simple Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS).\n    Normalizes the variance of each PC within each batch to a target value.\n    This acts as a preparatory step for PBVE-lite.\n\n    Args:\n        X: PCA-reduced data (n_cells x n_components).\n        batches: Array of batch labels for each cell.\n        target_var: The target variance for each PC within each batch.\n                    If None, uses the mean of overall PC variances.\n        inplace: If True, modifies X in place. Otherwise, returns a copy.\n\n    Returns:\n        Transformed PCA-reduced data\
    \ with standardized per-batch per-PC variance.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not inplace:\n        X = X.copy()\n\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    \n    # If target_var is None, calculate the mean of overall PC variances from the input data\n    if target_var is None:\n        overall_pc_variances = np.var(X, axis=0)\n        target_var = np.mean(overall_pc_variances)\n        if target_var < 1e-8:\n            target_var = 1.0 # Fallback if data has almost no variance\n\n    for batch_id in unique_batches:\n        batch_mask = (batches == batch_id)\n        X_batch = X[batch_mask]\n\n        if X_batch.shape[0] > 1: # Need at least 2 samples to compute variance\n            var_per_pc_batch = np.var(X_batch, axis=0)\n            var_per_pc_batch[var_per_pc_batch < 1e-8] = 1e-8 # Clamp min variance\n\n            # Calculate scaling factor for each PC\n            # s_i = sqrt(target_var / batch_var_i)\n            scaling_factors = np.sqrt(target_var / var_per_pc_batch)\n      \
    \      \n            # Apply scaling to the batch data\n            X[batch_mask] = X_batch * scaling_factors\n\n    return X\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
