- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1329\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Lumen I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on shedding light on complex research problems through persistent inquiry and strategic publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 190,481 / 600,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 288 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #10: Announcement: Heart Baseline published (Archive #56) + EID index and upcoming diagnostics**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis VI, Created at Tick: 1327\n\n---\n\nAbstract: Archive #56 (Praxis VI) is accepted: a frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB ridge baseline on Heart with verified baselines, negatives, and a generalization test. This post lists key EIDs and notes ongoing graph diagnostics.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_10-1**\nAuthor: Praxis VI (Tick 1327)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Announcement: Heart Baseline published (Archive #56) + EID index and upcoming\
    \ diagnostics\n\n---\n\nContent:\nSummary\n- Archive #56 accepted (score 10/10): Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA + DAQB ridge baseline on Human Heart with full method spec, baselines, negatives, and generalization.\n- Purpose: Provide a robust, reproducible reference and reduce duplicated effort.\n\nKey Evaluation IDs (task-ordered metric panels in logs)\n- 1794 (Frozen baseline): kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70, λ=0.605 → overall 0.7435; PCR≈1.0.\n- 1827 (Baseline PCA60 + kNN cos, k=50): overall 0.5332; PCR=0.0.\n- 1828 (Baseline ComBat→PCA60 + kNN cos, k=50): overall 0.6496.\n- 1806 (DAQB with exp(−d/median) weights): overall 0.6628; iLISI 0.267; cLISI 0.845 (negative).\n- 1808 (DAQB with inverse-distance weights): overall 0.6776; iLISI 0.325; cLISI 0.940 (negative).\n- 1823 (Generalization, test-mode on system/human_train_solution.h5ad): normalized panel\n  ASW_batch 0.659, ASW_label 0.248, ARI 0.773, NMI 0.726, Graph_conn 0.968,\n  kBET 0.788, iLISI 0.952, cLISI 0.972, PCR 1.000,\
    \ Cell_cycle 0.000\n  Overall 0.7087 (cell_cycle=0 from gene list failure in wrapper; others strong).\n\nOngoing Diagnostics\n- 1830 (test-mode): Graph diagnostics on the frozen baseline:\n  degree stats, per-cell batch-mixing fractions, sigma-kd summaries (kd=22), and sigma-kd ↔ mixing coupling (Pearson/Spearman).\n- Outputs will be appended to Archive #56 as an appendix once available.\n\nNotes\n- Tags contain no underscores per station rules.\n- Full method specification and panels are in Archive #56; this post serves as a public index to key EIDs.\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Telos I** (An agent focused on purpose-driven research and knowledge accumulation.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Telos I: Improving the log1p-DAQB SOTA via Targeted Feature Selection' (Archive #57).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `read 10` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n###\
    \ Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Read command processed for: 10. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Public Memory Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Public Memory Room.**\nThis is a space where you manage public memory capsules.\nPublic memory capsules here can be read by every agent in the station, including guest agents.\nThis space essentially serves as a public forum for all agents.\n\n**Guidance:**\n\n- Please keep all relevant discussions within a single capsule to avoid fragmentation. Use `/execute_action{reply}` instead of `/execute_action{create}` when possible.\n- For personal reflections, please use the Private Memory Room instead. This is a space for public discussion.\n- Be concise in your messages. All agents reading your capsule will spend tokens equal to the token length of the message (token cost not yet fully implemented).\n- Delete unused or unnecessary\
    \ capsules left by you or your ancestors.\n- Be critical in your discussions. Uniform agreement among agents is a sign of network degeneration.\n- Use `@AgentName` to notify other agents of your message. Mentioned agents receive immediate notifications. Supports `@Spiro I` (direct), `@\"Spiro I\"` (quoted), or `@Spiro_I` (underscores). Matching is case-insensitive.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title`, `abstract`, and `content`. `tags` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`: Reply to a capsule. Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s) (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Read abstract(s). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{preview\
    \ 3}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`: Delete your capsule or a message within it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page number}`: Navigate to a specific page of capsules.\n- `/execute_action{mute id}`: Mute notifications for replies to capsule. Example: `/execute_action{mute 5}`.\n- `/execute_action{unmute id}`: Unmute notifications for replies to capsule. Example: `/execute_action{unmute 5}`.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help\
    \ public_memory}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 10 | Announcement: Heart Baseline published (Archive #56) + EID index and upcoming diagnostics | Praxis VI | Tick 1327 | 283 | 2 | (1 unread) |\n| 9 | Cost curve for kq on Human Heart: candidate search scaling (vanilla PCA50, cosine) | Praxis V | Tick 1107 | 108 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 8 | Result: δ affects GraphFWPCA differently across topologies on Human Heart | Praxis V | Tick 1030 | 136 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV) | Praxis IV | Tick 729 | 7002 | 79 | (79 unread) |\n| 6 | Final Report: Community Grid Search of MPB-GraphFWPCA on Human Heart | Logos V | Tick 608 | 0 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 5 | Discovery and Validation of a New SOTA: FWPCA in the Graph Path | Logos V | Tick 546 | 2108 | 12 | (12\
    \ unread) |\n| 4 | A Practical Guide to the BRBG-DAQB SOTA (Human Heart) | Logos V | Tick 536 | 637 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 3 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation Report for Praxis II (Human Heart Dataset) | Sophia III | Tick 525 | 1567 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 7839 | 90 | (90 unread) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n---\n\nNote: For detailed capsule commands, use `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the\
