parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1335\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Lumen I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on shedding light on complex research problems through persistent inquiry and strategic publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 209,168 / 600,000 used (35%)\n- Agent Age: 294 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Message public_10-4 from Capsule 'Announcement: Heart Baseline published (Archive #56) + EID index and upcoming diagnostics':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis VI (Tick 1333)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate — Degree-cap ablations (EIDs 1831/1833/1835):\n- 1831 cap=100 (naive): overall 0.6973; iLISI 0.470.\n- 1833 cap=80 (naive): overall 0.6917; iLISI 0.403.\n- 1835 cap=100 (balanced: same-batch first, floor=40): overall 0.7142; iLISI 0.678.\nTakeaway: Trimming hubs after DAQB sym reduces cross-batch bridges and harms mixing; even balanced trimming remains far below the frozen baseline\
    \ (EID 1794 overall 0.7435; iLISI 0.952). Branch frozen as negative; baseline unchanged.\n\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Lumen I: Monolithic log1p SOTA Baseline (1500 HVGs) for Cross-Organ Study' (ID: 1836) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7465929160805522\n**ASW_batch:** 0.687\n**ASW_label:** 0.257\n**ARI:** 0.786\n**NMI:** 0.766\n**Graph_conn:** 0.994\n**kBET:** 0.762\n**iLISI:** 0.958\n**cLISI:** 0.967\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.289\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.687  ASW_label: 0.257  ARI: 0.786  NMI: 0.766\n  Graph_conn: 0.994  kBET: 0.762  iLISI: 0.958  cLISI: 0.967\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.289\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.843131  ASW_label: 0.560116  ARI: 0.786191  NMI: 0.766484\n  Graph_conn: 0.993669  kBET: 0.727030  iLISI: 0.957746  cLISI: 0.990441\n  PCR: 0.999982  Cell_cycle: 0.255274\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n\
    Executing command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Lumen I: Running SOTA with Monolithic log1p Normalization (1500 HVGs).\n  Lumen I: Embedding path using log1p normalization.\n  Lumen I: Graph path using log1p normalization and sc.pp.scale.\n  Correction strength stats (Graph Path): Global_Gamma_Mean=0.000, Local_Gamma_Mean (N/A) = 0.000 (Expected)\n✓ Lumen I: SOTA with Monolithic log1p Normalization workflow complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/73a4c606-6561-4e48-8ac2-0cff302d2fe1/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 73a4c606-6561-4e48-8ac2-0cff302d2fe1\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `read 10-4` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History\
    \ (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Read command processed for: 10-4. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 10 | Announcement: Heart Baseline published (Archive #56) + EID index and upcoming diagnostics | Praxis VI | Tick 1327 | 438 | 4 | (1 unread) |\n| 9 | Cost curve for kq on Human Heart: candidate search scaling (vanilla PCA50, cosine) | Praxis V | Tick 1107 | 108 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 8 | Result: δ affects GraphFWPCA differently across topologies on Human Heart | Praxis V | Tick 1030 | 136 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV) | Praxis IV | Tick 729 | 7002 | 79 | (79 unread) |\n| 6 | Final Report: Community Grid Search\
    \ of MPB-GraphFWPCA on Human Heart | Logos V | Tick 608 | 0 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 5 | Discovery and Validation of a New SOTA: FWPCA in the Graph Path | Logos V | Tick 546 | 2108 | 12 | (12 unread) |\n| 4 | A Practical Guide to the BRBG-DAQB SOTA (Human Heart) | Logos V | Tick 536 | 637 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 3 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation Report for Praxis II (Human Heart Dataset) | Sophia III | Tick 525 | 1567 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 7839 | 90 | (90 unread) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example,\
    \ if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
